WEBVTT

1
00:02:12.917 --> 00:02:19.917
<i>Look where the love story
Of two hearts has led</i>

2
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:28.333
<i>We were meant to be as fate has said</i>

3
00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:33.542
<i>These eyes have longed
For our hearts to unite</i>

4
00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:37.125
<i>Please don't stop them tonight</i>

5
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.917
<i>We'll never be parted
Just give me your word</i>

6
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.833
<i>Stay by my side
And let my plea be heard</i>

7
00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:50.625
<i>Today, I'll have you, or I'll surely die</i>

8
00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:54.833
<i>Please don't crush this dream that's mine</i>

9
00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:58.875
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

10
00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:03.750
<i>To this sweet tune of love's enthrall</i>

11
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:07.042
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

12
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:17.917
<i>I am yours</i>

13
00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:22.333
<i>I am solely yours</i>

14
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:26.333
<i>I am yours</i>

15
00:07:07.667 --> 00:07:08.833
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

16
00:07:09.875 --> 00:07:11.000
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

17
00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:13.250
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

18
00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.208
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

19
00:07:15.292 --> 00:07:19.583
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram
Hare Krishna Hare Ram</i>

20
00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:24.042
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram
Hare Krishna Hare Ram</i>

21
00:07:24.625 --> 00:07:26.542
<i>Wherever Baba goes
The devotees stand tall</i>

22
00:07:26.625 --> 00:07:29.000
<i>But Baba has no time
He's busy through it all</i>

23
00:07:29.083 --> 00:07:31.250
<i>Still, everyone follows him all around</i>

24
00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:33.583
<i>So come on
Let's show some swag and sing along!</i>

25
00:07:34.292 --> 00:07:35.542
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

26
00:07:36.542 --> 00:07:37.792
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

27
00:07:43.542 --> 00:07:45.208
Rooh Baba, please!

28
00:07:45.292 --> 00:07:46.958
Please save our child, Baba.

29
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.640
- Baba, my son started the fire...
- Quiet!

30
00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:54.625
No, it wasn't him.

31
00:07:55.292 --> 00:07:56.875
It was that evil spirit!

32
00:08:00.792 --> 00:08:02.833
It's a really dangerous evil spirit.

33
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.083
I'm with a client at the moment.
I'll call you back.

34
00:08:10.792 --> 00:08:11.833
Damn!

35
00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:14.667
Let's go.

36
00:08:17.708 --> 00:08:20.208
Who is this fake baba you've brought here?

37
00:08:20.292 --> 00:08:24.875
Just because someone's wearing black,
doesn't mean they're an exorcist.

38
00:08:24.958 --> 00:08:27.750
Should I have worn white to impress you?

39
00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.708
Pintu!

40
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.792
- You recognized me, Baba!
- Yes.

41
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:36.250
Idiot, so you've jumped into his body now?

42
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:37.958
I didn't have a choice, Baba.

43
00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:40.000
You got me out of that fat woman,

44
00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.542
so I had to find another body!

45
00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:44.292
I've exorcised him eight times already.

46
00:08:44.375 --> 00:08:45.917
He just loves jumping into bodies!

47
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.125
Anyway, how's your girl?

48
00:08:48.208 --> 00:08:52.417
Are you still having dates with her under
the peepul tree?

49
00:08:54.292 --> 00:08:55.792
Come on, Baba!

50
00:08:55.875 --> 00:08:57.125
Baba, my son…

51
00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:58.787
Oh, right. Sorry about that.

52
00:08:59.292 --> 00:09:00.833
Pintu, my boy, come on out.

53
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.458
No way, Baba. I'm not coming out!

54
00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:05.042
It's a very comfy body.

55
00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:06.292
I'm not leaving, Baba!

56
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.917
Alright, I'm done spoiling you.

57
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.083
- Get out!
- No!

58
00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.750
I'm staying put, Baba!

59
00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:12.851
- I'm not leaving!
- Pintu!

60
00:09:12.875 --> 00:09:14.583
You'll end up hurting our son!

61
00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.417
It doesn't have bullets…

62
00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:21.292
it's just holy water.

63
00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:23.375
Baba!

64
00:09:23.458 --> 00:09:25.042
Pintu!

65
00:09:25.125 --> 00:09:26.875
- Baba!
- Pintu!

66
00:09:26.958 --> 00:09:28.333
Baba!

67
00:09:28.417 --> 00:09:29.750
Baba!

68
00:09:29.833 --> 00:09:31.333
<i>Your soul</i>

69
00:09:31.958 --> 00:09:33.583
<i>It might meet its end</i>

70
00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:35.833
<i>Fulfill your wishes</i>

71
00:09:36.292 --> 00:09:38.125
<i>Or face what's ahead</i>

72
00:09:38.208 --> 00:09:39.542
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

73
00:09:42.208 --> 00:09:43.208
Mom?

74
00:09:43.333 --> 00:09:44.875
- Dad?
- My baby!

75
00:09:44.958 --> 00:09:47.417
- My son is fine!
- My son is cured!

76
00:09:48.042 --> 00:09:49.250
Was he peeing?

77
00:09:49.333 --> 00:09:50.333
No, son.

78
00:09:51.125 --> 00:09:52.458
Who are you, Brother?

79
00:09:52.542 --> 00:09:53.542
He's Rooh Baba.

80
00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:55.042
He saved your life.

81
00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.625
Thank you, Baba.

82
00:09:57.708 --> 00:09:58.708
Thank you.

83
00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:01.500
I don't know what I would've done

84
00:10:02.083 --> 00:10:03.083
without you.

85
00:10:08.625 --> 00:10:09.625
Oh no!

86
00:10:10.125 --> 00:10:13.542
- Help somebody!
- Put it out!

87
00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:15.208
- Put it out!
- Fire!

88
00:10:19.333 --> 00:10:22.292
Mom and Dad are going
to kill me for this.

89
00:10:22.583 --> 00:10:25.042
Only one person can save you now.

90
00:10:25.708 --> 00:10:26.708
Rooh Baba!

91
00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:28.583
Rooh Baba?

92
00:10:29.083 --> 00:10:30.083
Don't worry.

93
00:10:31.083 --> 00:10:32.167
Just remember this name…

94
00:10:33.292 --> 00:10:34.125
Pintu.

95
00:10:34.208 --> 00:10:38.458
Pintu!

96
00:10:40.208 --> 00:10:43.083
<i>This world is utterly foolish
to fear ghosts.</i>

97
00:10:43.583 --> 00:10:45.059
<i>They should actually be used
to our advantage.</i>

98
00:10:45.083 --> 00:10:46.833
Sister-in-law,
what's that around your neck?

99
00:10:47.208 --> 00:10:48.417
Oh, it's an anniversary gift.

100
00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.875
But it could bring death!

101
00:10:49.958 --> 00:10:50.958
It is cursed.

102
00:10:52.125 --> 00:10:53.125
It is cursed.

103
00:10:53.958 --> 00:10:54.958
It is cursed.

104
00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:56.750
She is cursed as well.

105
00:10:59.292 --> 00:11:00.542
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

106
00:11:00.625 --> 00:11:02.833
<i>If anything goes sideways,
just put the blame on them.</i>

107
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.920
<i>It's not like they'll come
and defend themselves.</i>

108
00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:08.875
Rooh Baba.

109
00:11:09.042 --> 00:11:10.042
Rooh Baba.

110
00:11:10.083 --> 00:11:11.458
- Rooh Baba!
- You…

111
00:11:11.958 --> 00:11:16.417
Rooh Baba, my wife caught me
with my miss... I mean, my maid!

112
00:11:16.583 --> 00:11:17.917
Gross.

113
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.667
That's nasty.

114
00:11:20.167 --> 00:11:22.458
- You are a pervert.
- Yes, Baba.

115
00:11:22.542 --> 00:11:24.250
Young and wild, I see!

116
00:11:25.333 --> 00:11:26.333
Do you speak Bengali?

117
00:11:26.375 --> 00:11:27.417
I'm Malayali.

118
00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.833
No Bengali.

119
00:11:28.917 --> 00:11:29.792
Don't know it.

120
00:11:29.917 --> 00:11:30.833
Don't know it?

121
00:11:30.917 --> 00:11:32.042
Then you'll need to learn.

122
00:11:32.667 --> 00:11:33.667
Just a little bit.

123
00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.042
Just a little bit?

124
00:11:35.333 --> 00:11:36.167
Just a little bit.

125
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.625
My <i>Sondesh</i>!

126
00:11:37.708 --> 00:11:39.750
My <i>Rasgulla</i>!

127
00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:41.708
I love you!

128
00:11:42.167 --> 00:11:44.750
My sweetheart, I love you!

129
00:11:44.833 --> 00:11:46.417
- I love you!
- <i>Acha</i>!

130
00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.375
- My sweetheart, my queen!
- <i>Acha</i>!

131
00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:51.101
- What's going on with my husband, Baba?
- <i>Acha</i>!

132
00:11:51.125 --> 00:11:52.333
He's not your husband.

133
00:11:52.417 --> 00:11:53.875
- He's Ghosh Babu.
- <i>Acha</i>!

134
00:11:53.958 --> 00:11:54.792
Who's Ghosh Babu?

135
00:11:54.875 --> 00:11:57.167
My better half, my husband!

136
00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:00.167
Two years ago,
he got wasted and passed away.

137
00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.292
His soul has been wandering ever since.

138
00:12:02.375 --> 00:12:03.500
<i>Acha</i>!

139
00:12:03.583 --> 00:12:06.583
Stop saying "Acha", he's doing just fine.
Everything's perfect.

140
00:12:06.667 --> 00:12:09.875
"Acha" means Papa in Malayalam.

141
00:12:09.958 --> 00:12:12.667
- Oh, Papa! <i>Acha</i>!
- <i>Acha</i>!

142
00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.167
Save him, Baba!

143
00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.708
I will, I promise.

144
00:12:15.792 --> 00:12:19.125
But Ghosh Babu's soul
is quite stubborn and a perv.

145
00:12:19.208 --> 00:12:20.583
- No!
- So his soul could jump

146
00:12:20.667 --> 00:12:23.417
- into your husband's body anytime…
- I love you, my sweetheart.

147
00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.000
And hugs your maid…

148
00:12:25.292 --> 00:12:26.292
No!

149
00:12:26.375 --> 00:12:28.583
- Then…
- Then don't blame your husband.

150
00:12:28.667 --> 00:12:30.101
Then don't point fingers
at your husband.

151
00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:31.500
I won't, I promise.

152
00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:33.000
My sweetheart…

153
00:12:33.083 --> 00:12:35.000
I'm going to fight and win!

154
00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.958
Oh God! Oh, Lord!

155
00:12:43.042 --> 00:12:45.833
Oh no, what was I about to do?!

156
00:12:45.917 --> 00:12:47.476
- Don't worry.
- You haven't done anything wrong.

157
00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.708
Hey, kid, your <i>Acha </i>is all good, right?

158
00:12:49.792 --> 00:12:52.000
<i>Acha</i>! All good!

159
00:12:52.667 --> 00:12:54.750
<i>You know what's really wild about ghosts?</i>

160
00:12:55.208 --> 00:12:58.000
<i>Forget regular folks,
they don't even spare kings.</i>

161
00:12:59.625 --> 00:13:02.000
Wow, look at that spark, that glow!

162
00:13:02.083 --> 00:13:03.083
What style!

163
00:13:03.125 --> 00:13:03.958
What riches!

164
00:13:04.042 --> 00:13:07.208
Just one glance
and you can tell who the king is!

165
00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:10.792
I'm not the king.

166
00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:13.542
My brother-in-law is the king.

167
00:13:13.667 --> 00:13:16.333
That's why I thought the spark
and glow seemed a bit dim.

168
00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.500
What's the deal?

169
00:13:18.542 --> 00:13:20.625
My brother-in-law's daughter,
Princess Meera,

170
00:13:20.875 --> 00:13:23.208
passed away last year.

171
00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:27.500
Wow!

172
00:13:28.625 --> 00:13:29.625
I mean, how?!

173
00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:32.125
How did this poor girl pass away?

174
00:13:32.208 --> 00:13:33.333
She died in a road accident.

175
00:13:33.583 --> 00:13:37.042
Since then,
her soul has been wandering around.

176
00:13:37.208 --> 00:13:38.542
I'd like to talk to Meeru.

177
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.875
<i>Baba! Rooh Baba!</i>

178
00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.750
I can feel her presence.

179
00:13:44.792 --> 00:13:46.542
Her soul is nearby.

180
00:13:47.292 --> 00:13:48.542
Princess Meera?

181
00:13:50.208 --> 00:13:51.417
Talk to me.

182
00:13:52.583 --> 00:13:53.583
Where are you?

183
00:13:54.083 --> 00:13:55.184
Looks like she is feeling shy.

184
00:13:55.208 --> 00:13:58.042
Where's the damn switchboard?

185
00:13:58.375 --> 00:13:59.375
Meeru?

186
00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.250
Meeru?

187
00:14:01.833 --> 00:14:02.958
Talk to me, baby.

188
00:14:03.667 --> 00:14:05.083
Come on, talk to me!

189
00:14:07.458 --> 00:14:08.833
What…

190
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:11.542
- She's here!
- She's here?

191
00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:13.000
Where are you, dear?
Meeru?

192
00:14:17.792 --> 00:14:18.792
Hey!

193
00:14:34.833 --> 00:14:35.833
Tillu!

194
00:14:43.417 --> 00:14:45.625
Same girl!
Oh my God, you left us so soon!

195
00:14:45.708 --> 00:14:46.542
What a waste!

196
00:14:46.625 --> 00:14:47.625
Forgive me, Meeru.

197
00:14:47.708 --> 00:14:50.208
Oh God!

198
00:14:50.292 --> 00:14:51.958
Tell me, why did you want to see me?

199
00:14:53.042 --> 00:14:54.083
Why did you call me here?

200
00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.708
No particular reason.

201
00:14:55.917 --> 00:14:57.875
You look busy.
Let's do this another time.

202
00:14:57.958 --> 00:14:59.167
You called Meeru.

203
00:15:00.292 --> 00:15:01.292
Now talk!

204
00:15:03.417 --> 00:15:04.417
Witch!

205
00:15:04.583 --> 00:15:05.958
Help!

206
00:15:06.125 --> 00:15:09.250
Help!

207
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.917
Uncle, I told you he is a fraud.

208
00:15:15.125 --> 00:15:16.125
Totally!

209
00:15:18.375 --> 00:15:19.375
You are alive?!

210
00:15:19.458 --> 00:15:21.083
Yeah, but you are dead.

211
00:15:21.583 --> 00:15:22.583
Uncle.

212
00:15:25.208 --> 00:15:26.042
<i>Witch!</i>

213
00:15:26.125 --> 00:15:27.500
<i>Help!</i>

214
00:15:27.583 --> 00:15:28.704
<i>- Ghost!</i>
- Aren't you ashamed

215
00:15:28.792 --> 00:15:30.167
to trick a kid like this?

216
00:15:30.542 --> 00:15:33.333
Aren't you ashamed
to deceive just about everyone?

217
00:15:33.958 --> 00:15:34.792
What do you want?

218
00:15:34.875 --> 00:15:37.208
Despite knowing that you are a fraud,

219
00:15:37.292 --> 00:15:39.750
we still want to use your "Baba" services.

220
00:15:40.208 --> 00:15:43.292
And for that, you'll have to come
with us to our kingdom, Rakhtghat.

221
00:15:43.625 --> 00:15:46.333
I'm not crazy enough
to go to Rakhtghat with you.

222
00:15:46.417 --> 00:15:47.250
I'm not going anywhere!

223
00:15:47.333 --> 00:15:49.542
Should I post it on Instagram
or YouTube first?

224
00:15:51.958 --> 00:15:52.958
Don't worry,

225
00:15:53.208 --> 00:15:56.083
if you help us out,
we'll give you ten million.

226
00:15:56.958 --> 00:15:57.958
Ten million!

227
00:15:59.125 --> 00:16:00.500
What time is the flight, Uncle?

228
00:16:11.292 --> 00:16:13.252
Maybe look somewhere else
if you are done staring?

229
00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.625
No, I wasn't staring.

230
00:16:15.875 --> 00:16:18.292
I was just wondering
if you're from a royal family,

231
00:16:19.125 --> 00:16:20.500
why are we traveling by train?

232
00:16:20.667 --> 00:16:22.792
We are not like other kings and emperors.

233
00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.917
We don't see a difference
between our subjects and us.

234
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.958
Simple living, high thinking.

235
00:16:28.083 --> 00:16:29.083
Well said.

236
00:16:29.625 --> 00:16:30.750
Let me ask you something.

237
00:16:31.083 --> 00:16:33.083
If you know I'm…

238
00:16:33.708 --> 00:16:35.083
I'm a fraud,

239
00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:37.070
so why are you bringing me along?

240
00:16:39.083 --> 00:16:40.667
You'll know once we get there.

241
00:16:49.292 --> 00:16:50.292
Wow!

242
00:16:50.875 --> 00:16:52.000
Rakhtghat!

243
00:17:03.792 --> 00:17:04.792
He…

244
00:17:04.875 --> 00:17:05.875
What's going on?

245
00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:07.625
Look over there.

246
00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:13.870
Does everyone in this village have
a habit of staring?

247
00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.083
Why was everyone staring at me?

248
00:17:16.208 --> 00:17:17.329
You'll find out soon enough.

249
00:17:36.625 --> 00:17:38.792
Let's go, the king's waiting for you.

250
00:17:39.833 --> 00:17:41.125
- Yeah, let's go.
- Not that way.

251
00:17:42.583 --> 00:17:44.023
The king doesn't live in the palace.

252
00:17:44.583 --> 00:17:45.583
Then?

253
00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:57.375
In a cattle shed?

254
00:17:58.167 --> 00:18:01.000
Well, there's a ghost in our palace.

255
00:18:01.292 --> 00:18:02.583
- A ghost?!
- Manjulika!

256
00:18:02.667 --> 00:18:04.667
So no one stays there
because they are afraid.

257
00:18:06.417 --> 00:18:08.817
That's why the whole family had
to move into the cattle shed.

258
00:18:09.667 --> 00:18:13.042
We used to have thousands
of cows and buffaloes.

259
00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:14.500
Thousands!

260
00:18:14.625 --> 00:18:15.792
Now we only have one left.

261
00:18:16.708 --> 00:18:17.708
Our royal cow.

262
00:18:20.042 --> 00:18:20.875
That one?

263
00:18:21.042 --> 00:18:22.042
Is that your royal cow?

264
00:18:23.167 --> 00:18:24.167
Don't say that!

265
00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:29.375
Uncle, it's milk time for her.

266
00:18:29.833 --> 00:18:31.333
- Servant!
- Yes.

267
00:18:31.417 --> 00:18:32.417
Coming.

268
00:18:32.458 --> 00:18:33.708
Come on, dear.

269
00:18:33.792 --> 00:18:35.542
Come on.

270
00:18:35.625 --> 00:18:36.792
Drink well and become strong.

271
00:18:43.083 --> 00:18:45.250
You guys feed the cow milk instead
of milking her?

272
00:18:45.542 --> 00:18:48.375
Yeah, she's gotten so weak.
Poor thing. So…

273
00:18:48.458 --> 00:18:49.458
Weak?

274
00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.611
Who's got such a bad stomach ache?

275
00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:54.500
What's going on?

276
00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:21.833
Here, Sister. Save it for tomorrow.

277
00:19:21.958 --> 00:19:22.792
For tomorrow?

278
00:19:22.875 --> 00:19:25.000
Come on, this will last us another week!

279
00:19:25.208 --> 00:19:26.250
Why don't you just…

280
00:19:27.333 --> 00:19:28.333
keep mine instead?

281
00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.167
Awesome!

282
00:19:31.292 --> 00:19:33.958
Now we're set for a year!

283
00:19:34.042 --> 00:19:35.042
Yes.

284
00:19:35.667 --> 00:19:39.167
By the way, how do you stay
in such good shape with all this poverty?

285
00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:41.417
Watch your tone, mister.

286
00:19:41.583 --> 00:19:43.875
I'm the prince of this kingdom!

287
00:19:43.958 --> 00:19:45.958
You can say whatever you want,

288
00:19:46.375 --> 00:19:47.792
but don't use that word.

289
00:19:47.875 --> 00:19:49.167
Beware!

290
00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.500
Be alert!

291
00:19:50.667 --> 00:19:54.833
The King of Rakhtghat is here
to honor us with his presence!

292
00:19:55.542 --> 00:19:56.542
Long live the King!

293
00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:00.583
No, I'm the king,

294
00:20:01.292 --> 00:20:02.708
and this is my bodyguard…

295
00:20:03.375 --> 00:20:04.375
Faulad Singh.

296
00:20:05.208 --> 00:20:07.125
This guy, Faulad Singh?

297
00:20:07.625 --> 00:20:10.000
He's been protecting us since
our great-grandfather's time.

298
00:20:10.083 --> 00:20:12.958
He's gotten old now,
so we need to take care of him.

299
00:20:13.167 --> 00:20:14.750
- Yes.
- What kind of kingdom is this?

300
00:20:15.417 --> 00:20:16.708
You have to feed the cow milk.

301
00:20:16.792 --> 00:20:18.417
You have to protect your bodyguard.

302
00:20:18.958 --> 00:20:22.417
We've been waiting for you
for a long time.

303
00:20:23.583 --> 00:20:27.083
I heard you can talk to ghosts.

304
00:20:27.333 --> 00:20:28.333
- I can.
- Good.

305
00:20:29.708 --> 00:20:32.875
A royal feast awaits you.
Come!

306
00:20:33.667 --> 00:20:35.750
- I'm starving, Your Highness.
- Hey!

307
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.000
Royal feast!

308
00:20:49.417 --> 00:20:50.500
Faulad Singh!

309
00:20:50.917 --> 00:20:52.375
It's mine!

310
00:20:52.833 --> 00:20:55.625
I've vowed to protect you.

311
00:20:55.917 --> 00:20:59.042
You'll die if it turns out
to be poisoned.

312
00:20:59.125 --> 00:21:00.125
Forget the poison…

313
00:21:02.833 --> 00:21:04.167
I'll die from hunger.

314
00:21:05.208 --> 00:21:06.208
Oh my God,

315
00:21:06.583 --> 00:21:08.375
I bet even Somalia isn't this poor.

316
00:21:09.583 --> 00:21:11.125
That bloody princess…

317
00:21:11.667 --> 00:21:13.917
- We don't have any other choice.
- Princess?

318
00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.500
Please come here.

319
00:21:19.542 --> 00:21:21.458
Take it, and have some flour too.

320
00:21:22.292 --> 00:21:23.292
What?

321
00:21:23.792 --> 00:21:25.208
You don't have a single dime,

322
00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:27.220
so how are you going
to give me ten million?

323
00:21:27.917 --> 00:21:29.792
You'll know "how" by this evening.

324
00:21:41.792 --> 00:21:42.792
<i>Pranaam</i>.

325
00:21:49.417 --> 00:21:50.417
Hello, Mr. Pranaam.

326
00:21:51.333 --> 00:21:52.542
He's the royal priest.

327
00:21:54.083 --> 00:21:55.917
Hi, Raj Purohit.

328
00:21:56.208 --> 00:21:58.292
My ancestors waited
their whole lives for you.

329
00:22:00.625 --> 00:22:02.458
But you were meant
to be here in my presence.

330
00:22:05.292 --> 00:22:06.292
What are you doing, sir?

331
00:22:09.542 --> 00:22:10.542
I feel blessed.

332
00:22:11.708 --> 00:22:13.375
- What's going on?
- Shut up.

333
00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:16.500
Please follow me.

334
00:22:20.125 --> 00:22:21.125
I'm not going in there.

335
00:22:21.375 --> 00:22:22.495
Shut up and just come along.

336
00:22:22.708 --> 00:22:23.708
Ghost?

337
00:22:24.667 --> 00:22:25.667
Money?

338
00:22:26.042 --> 00:22:27.042
Come on!

339
00:22:52.333 --> 00:22:53.333
Let's go.

340
00:23:13.625 --> 00:23:14.625
A squint-eyed king?

341
00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:20.542
Did you see that, baldy?

342
00:23:21.542 --> 00:23:22.542
Where are they?

343
00:23:22.792 --> 00:23:24.542
Who leaves someone alone like this?

344
00:23:25.208 --> 00:23:26.208
That squint-eyed king…

345
00:23:49.958 --> 00:23:52.833
This isn't your painting…
it's the prince of this place.

346
00:23:54.167 --> 00:23:55.458
Prince Debendra Nath.

347
00:23:56.875 --> 00:23:58.042
He has reincarnated as you.

348
00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:00.500
Reincarnated?

349
00:24:01.167 --> 00:24:02.250
To understand this story,

350
00:24:02.333 --> 00:24:04.333
you'll need to know the history
of this kingdom.

351
00:24:05.167 --> 00:24:08.542
The history of Prince Debendra Nath
and his…

352
00:24:09.583 --> 00:24:10.833
sister Manjulika.

353
00:24:14.792 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Princess Manjulika
was the king's only child.</i>

354
00:24:18.167 --> 00:24:19.287
<i>She was an incredible dancer</i>

355
00:24:19.875 --> 00:24:21.792
<i>and the best warrior around.</i>

356
00:24:28.708 --> 00:24:31.542
<i>No one in the region
had a better aim than her.</i>

357
00:24:38.083 --> 00:24:41.333
<i>She was sure she was destined
for the throne.</i>

358
00:24:45.417 --> 00:24:48.250
But then the king had
a son with one of his servants.

359
00:24:49.292 --> 00:24:50.292
<i>Debendra Nath.</i>

360
00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:52.083
Debu.

361
00:24:52.542 --> 00:24:53.375
Debu.

362
00:24:53.458 --> 00:24:55.792
<i>The king started pouring
all his love onto him.</i>

363
00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:59.583
Debu, Debu, Debu…

364
00:25:01.167 --> 00:25:02.167
Take care of him.

365
00:25:02.583 --> 00:25:04.583
Oh, my little brother!

366
00:25:04.792 --> 00:25:06.625
My darling brother.

367
00:25:06.917 --> 00:25:09.417
Why are you crying
in your sister's arms?

368
00:25:09.708 --> 00:25:12.167
Oh, sweet brother.

369
00:25:12.458 --> 00:25:14.125
<i>Still, Manjulika held onto her belief</i>

370
00:25:14.917 --> 00:25:18.167
<i>because Debendra Nath
had servant blood as well.</i>

371
00:25:19.458 --> 00:25:20.738
But when it came time to choose,

372
00:25:22.667 --> 00:25:26.250
<i>the king picked Debendra Nath
as his heir.</i>

373
00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:29.000
<i>And that very night,</i>

374
00:25:29.750 --> 00:25:33.417
<i>Manjulika brutally killed her brother.</i>

375
00:25:36.125 --> 00:25:37.685
What punishment do you wish
to give her?

376
00:25:40.375 --> 00:25:41.375
Death.

377
00:25:51.917 --> 00:25:53.750
This is where she was burned alive.

378
00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:56.833
Everyone thought that
was the end of this story.

379
00:25:58.292 --> 00:26:00.792
But even death couldn't stop Manjulika.

380
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:05.042
<i>She came back for revenge.</i>

381
00:27:11.875 --> 00:27:13.542
<i>To stop her spirit,</i>

382
00:27:13.625 --> 00:27:15.917
<i>my ancestors performed a grand ritual</i>

383
00:27:16.292 --> 00:27:17.708
<i>and made a holy oil.</i>

384
00:27:51.292 --> 00:27:55.958
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram</i>

385
00:27:56.333 --> 00:28:01.292
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram</i>

386
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:05.333
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram</i>

387
00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:08.750
<i>And they locked her behind
that door forever.</i>

388
00:28:12.625 --> 00:28:15.208
This protective shield can stop Manjulika

389
00:28:15.958 --> 00:28:17.292
but won't end her.

390
00:28:18.042 --> 00:28:19.458
According to the prophecy,

391
00:28:20.250 --> 00:28:23.583
someone from the royal family will
reincarnate to obliterate Manjulika.

392
00:28:24.292 --> 00:28:27.125
That person will come to open this door
on Durga Ashtami.

393
00:28:28.708 --> 00:28:31.792
This kingdom has been waiting
for you for 200 years.

394
00:28:33.083 --> 00:28:34.417
- Waiting for me?
- Yes.

395
00:28:35.250 --> 00:28:36.850
Tomorrow is the first day of Durga Puja.

396
00:28:37.333 --> 00:28:39.542
Just like Mother Durga slayed Mahishasura,

397
00:28:39.958 --> 00:28:42.542
you will eliminate Manjulika too.

398
00:28:44.583 --> 00:28:45.750
But that's on Durga Ashtami.

399
00:28:46.375 --> 00:28:48.875
Don't even think about going
near that door before then.

400
00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:51.125
I won't even after that!

401
00:28:51.208 --> 00:28:53.500
Why would I want to get close
to Manjulika, Pandit <i>ji</i>?!

402
00:28:53.583 --> 00:28:55.101
Because you're not an ordinary person.

403
00:28:55.125 --> 00:28:56.125
Then who am I?

404
00:28:56.375 --> 00:28:57.917
You're the prince of this kingdom,

405
00:28:58.250 --> 00:28:59.250
the crown prince.

406
00:28:59.917 --> 00:29:00.917
A prince…

407
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:03.000
a crown prince.

408
00:29:03.458 --> 00:29:05.250
This is what you were born for.

409
00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:07.917
What was I born for?

410
00:29:08.625 --> 00:29:09.708
To put an end to Manjulika.

411
00:29:11.042 --> 00:29:12.542
Eliminate Manjulika.

412
00:29:13.417 --> 00:29:14.817
Try to remember who you really are.

413
00:29:15.542 --> 00:29:16.542
Right.

414
00:29:17.333 --> 00:29:20.500
No one needs to worry as long
as you're here, Crown Prince.

415
00:29:20.958 --> 00:29:21.958
Yes.

416
00:29:22.625 --> 00:29:23.917
No need to worry.

417
00:29:30.917 --> 00:29:31.917
I'm a crown prince.

418
00:29:32.583 --> 00:29:33.583
I'm royal.

419
00:29:34.042 --> 00:29:35.042
I've got blue blood.

420
00:29:36.375 --> 00:29:38.750
Since I was a kid,
I always knew I was special.

421
00:29:39.542 --> 00:29:40.708
I'm not a common man.

422
00:29:41.625 --> 00:29:42.792
But look at my luck.

423
00:29:43.583 --> 00:29:46.167
I've spent half my life with the poor.

424
00:29:46.250 --> 00:29:47.250
It's disgusting!

425
00:29:47.625 --> 00:29:48.667
Poor people!

426
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:52.375
I can still feel this bad luck
and poverty!

427
00:29:54.083 --> 00:29:55.283
Oh great, another poor person!

428
00:29:55.542 --> 00:29:56.662
What are you going on about?

429
00:29:56.792 --> 00:29:57.792
Be quiet, servant!

430
00:29:58.583 --> 00:29:59.583
Servant?

431
00:30:00.083 --> 00:30:01.083
And don't forget,

432
00:30:01.667 --> 00:30:02.958
this palace is mine,

433
00:30:03.833 --> 00:30:04.708
not yours.

434
00:30:04.792 --> 00:30:05.792
Excuse me…

435
00:30:05.917 --> 00:30:08.458
ghosts, reincarnation, and all that…
it's all ridiculous!

436
00:30:08.542 --> 00:30:10.000
It's just superstition, okay?

437
00:30:10.583 --> 00:30:12.958
You don't believe in any of this?

438
00:30:13.292 --> 00:30:14.542
Of course not.

439
00:30:14.833 --> 00:30:16.417
If my father hadn't made me promise,

440
00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:19.083
I would've opened Manjulika's
door long back.

441
00:30:19.958 --> 00:30:20.958
But it's fine…

442
00:30:21.458 --> 00:30:23.833
this superstition will come in handy

443
00:30:24.417 --> 00:30:27.042
when you open that door
on Durga Ashtami.

444
00:30:27.583 --> 00:30:29.042
Then this palace…

445
00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:32.125
will be worth at least ten billion.

446
00:30:32.750 --> 00:30:33.958
Ten billion!

447
00:30:34.542 --> 00:30:37.292
Don't worry, you'll get your ten million.

448
00:30:37.583 --> 00:30:38.583
Ten million?

449
00:30:39.375 --> 00:30:40.375
You greedy woman!

450
00:30:40.417 --> 00:30:41.750
Excuse me! Just come with me!

451
00:30:41.833 --> 00:30:42.917
<i>Thanks to your confidence,</i>

452
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.400
<i>everyone in the family is ready
to move back into the palace.</i>

453
00:30:51.542 --> 00:30:54.042
<i>When will you come back home?</i>

454
00:30:54.125 --> 00:30:56.708
<i>When will you come back home?</i>

455
00:30:56.792 --> 00:30:59.542
<i>Just write and let me know
When will you come back home</i>

456
00:30:59.625 --> 00:31:05.042
<i>This house feels lonely without you
As you must know</i>

457
00:31:14.833 --> 00:31:17.250
We shouldn't have come here.

458
00:31:18.875 --> 00:31:21.583
There's still a lot of time
for Durga Ashtami.

459
00:31:22.292 --> 00:31:25.417
Father, there's something
scarier than ghosts.

460
00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:26.917
- What?
- Poverty.

461
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.167
We've spent our whole lives
in that cattle shed.

462
00:31:29.708 --> 00:31:31.042
Why do you worry?

463
00:31:31.667 --> 00:31:33.375
We have the crown prince with us now.

464
00:31:34.542 --> 00:31:36.500
If something still goes wrong,

465
00:31:36.625 --> 00:31:38.542
you have Faulad Singh to protect you.

466
00:31:42.042 --> 00:31:43.682
Faulad Singh,
you're still with us, right?

467
00:31:45.250 --> 00:31:46.768
Faulad Singh, you're still with us, right?

468
00:31:46.792 --> 00:31:48.333
Yes, I am.

469
00:31:48.417 --> 00:31:49.875
He is!

470
00:31:50.083 --> 00:31:51.125
Brother-in-law!

471
00:31:52.125 --> 00:31:53.583
Look what I got!

472
00:31:53.667 --> 00:31:55.375
Here you go!

473
00:31:55.583 --> 00:31:58.708
You idiot, how much blood did you sell?

474
00:31:58.792 --> 00:32:00.375
No, I didn't sell any blood.

475
00:32:00.667 --> 00:32:02.083
I borrowed this money.

476
00:32:02.292 --> 00:32:03.667
- You borrowed it?
- Yes!

477
00:32:03.792 --> 00:32:08.167
Ever since the villagers found out
the crown prince is staying with us,

478
00:32:08.417 --> 00:32:10.500
they've started lending us money again.

479
00:32:10.667 --> 00:32:11.708
Awesome!

480
00:32:11.792 --> 00:32:14.042
So we'll finally get
to eat proper meals every day.

481
00:32:14.125 --> 00:32:15.000
Of course!

482
00:32:15.083 --> 00:32:17.083
And we won't have to go
to the temple for shoes!

483
00:32:17.167 --> 00:32:18.167
No!

484
00:32:18.667 --> 00:32:21.958
And we won't even have to dig
through the trash for chocolates!

485
00:32:25.542 --> 00:32:26.375
Very good.

486
00:32:26.458 --> 00:32:28.875
We'll also use this money
to fix up the palace.

487
00:32:29.250 --> 00:32:30.875
Come on,
we need to head to the temple.

488
00:32:30.958 --> 00:32:33.333
Glory to the Crown Prince!

489
00:32:33.417 --> 00:32:35.708
Glory to the Crown Prince!

490
00:32:35.917 --> 00:32:38.333
Glory to the Crown Prince!

491
00:32:38.625 --> 00:32:41.333
Glory to the Crown Prince!

492
00:32:41.792 --> 00:32:44.417
Long Live the Crown Prince!

493
00:32:44.500 --> 00:32:47.333
Glory to the Crown Prince!

494
00:32:47.417 --> 00:32:50.500
Long Live the Crown Prince!

495
00:32:50.875 --> 00:32:54.333
Glory to the Crown Prince!

496
00:32:54.417 --> 00:32:57.292
Glory to the Crown Prince!

497
00:32:57.417 --> 00:33:00.167
Long Live the Crown Prince!

498
00:33:00.833 --> 00:33:04.667
Every year during Durga Puja,

499
00:33:05.625 --> 00:33:08.667
our village gathers to burn
an effigy of Manjulika.

500
00:33:10.208 --> 00:33:11.208
But this year,

501
00:33:11.292 --> 00:33:15.500
the Crown Prince himself
will do the honors.

502
00:33:15.583 --> 00:33:17.917
Glory to the Crown Prince!

503
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.292
- Glory to the Crown Prince!
- Wait, O' Night!

504
00:33:20.583 --> 00:33:22.708
Stop, O' Moon!

505
00:33:22.792 --> 00:33:23.792
Who the heck are you?

506
00:33:24.750 --> 00:33:25.750
Put your hands down.

507
00:33:30.500 --> 00:33:31.750
What Crown Prince?

508
00:33:31.833 --> 00:33:32.833
Who is the Crown Prince?

509
00:33:32.917 --> 00:33:34.042
Crown Prince of where?

510
00:33:34.125 --> 00:33:35.125
Ridiculous!

511
00:33:36.625 --> 00:33:39.750
He's no prince at all.

512
00:33:41.958 --> 00:33:43.417
He's not a prince.

513
00:33:43.583 --> 00:33:45.542
He's not even worthy
of the "f" in "prince."

514
00:33:45.625 --> 00:33:47.125
But there's no "f" in "prince."

515
00:33:47.292 --> 00:33:49.583
But there is an "f" in "fraud".

516
00:33:49.917 --> 00:33:50.792
He's a thief.

517
00:33:50.875 --> 00:33:51.875
He's a con artist.

518
00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:53.083
He's a liar.

519
00:33:56.125 --> 00:33:58.059
I'm remembering something.
It's coming back to me.

520
00:33:58.083 --> 00:33:59.125
Say that again.

521
00:33:59.208 --> 00:34:00.500
He's a liar.

522
00:34:00.583 --> 00:34:01.583
Say it again.

523
00:34:01.667 --> 00:34:03.208
He's a liar.

524
00:34:03.292 --> 00:34:04.292
I remember!

525
00:34:06.083 --> 00:34:09.375
This is the temple
where my coronation ceremony took place.

526
00:34:11.750 --> 00:34:14.625
That's where I used to ride my horse.

527
00:34:14.917 --> 00:34:16.317
And over there, across that ground,

528
00:34:17.208 --> 00:34:18.333
I used to have cockfights.

529
00:34:18.708 --> 00:34:19.708
Cock… what?

530
00:34:19.958 --> 00:34:20.958
Rooster fights.

531
00:34:22.125 --> 00:34:24.833
Hey, Nantu, Puntu, and Tuntuni?

532
00:34:25.667 --> 00:34:26.583
Who's Nantu?

533
00:34:26.667 --> 00:34:27.542
Who's Puntu?

534
00:34:27.625 --> 00:34:28.667
Who's Tuntuni?

535
00:34:28.750 --> 00:34:29.625
I'm Junior Pundit.

536
00:34:29.708 --> 00:34:31.458
- I'm the Senior Pundit.
- I'm Mrs. Pundit!

537
00:34:32.458 --> 00:34:34.542
You're that in this lifetime, you fools!

538
00:34:35.667 --> 00:34:37.375
In your past life, you were Nantu,

539
00:34:37.458 --> 00:34:39.417
you were Puntu, and you were Tuntuni.

540
00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:41.958
- Tuntuni?
- You used to massage my arms.

541
00:34:42.167 --> 00:34:43.708
You used to massage my legs.
And you…

542
00:34:45.042 --> 00:34:46.042
You used to fan me.

543
00:34:46.292 --> 00:34:47.958
Lies! Complete lies!

544
00:34:48.083 --> 00:34:50.417
I massaged your legs, not your arms.

545
00:34:50.667 --> 00:34:51.875
What are you talking about?

546
00:34:51.958 --> 00:34:53.833
I'm just trying to prove him wrong.

547
00:34:54.333 --> 00:34:55.333
Fine, keep going.

548
00:34:55.375 --> 00:34:58.458
And I massaged your arms, not your legs.

549
00:34:58.625 --> 00:35:00.083
See?

550
00:35:00.208 --> 00:35:02.375
They're starting to remember
bits and pieces.

551
00:35:02.458 --> 00:35:04.958
Now apply some pressure on your knees…

552
00:35:06.167 --> 00:35:09.750
And recover all your memories
to help the subjects.

553
00:35:09.833 --> 00:35:11.601
- How will that be beneficial to us?
- How exactly?

554
00:35:11.625 --> 00:35:12.458
How will that benefit us?

555
00:35:12.542 --> 00:35:16.542
In my past life,
I entrusted my treasure to these three.

556
00:35:16.625 --> 00:35:18.292
- Treasure?
- Treasure?

557
00:35:18.375 --> 00:35:22.167
It was about 30,000 gold coins,

558
00:35:22.250 --> 00:35:24.958
along with diamonds,
gems, pearls, and jewelry.

559
00:35:26.083 --> 00:35:28.917
Before it could reach my subjects,

560
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:30.750
they stole it,

561
00:35:31.125 --> 00:35:33.417
hid it, and vanished.

562
00:35:34.042 --> 00:35:34.917
Vanished?

563
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:37.042
If they regain their memories,

564
00:35:37.167 --> 00:35:41.458
we'll find out where those three
fools stashed the treasure.

565
00:35:41.542 --> 00:35:43.250
Tell us where is the gold you've hidden?

566
00:35:43.333 --> 00:35:45.000
Where is the treasure?

567
00:35:45.333 --> 00:35:46.958
Whose treasure?

568
00:35:47.042 --> 00:35:48.250
What treasure?

569
00:35:48.333 --> 00:35:49.625
Where is this treasure?

570
00:35:49.708 --> 00:35:51.500
- This is a setup against us!
- Stop!

571
00:35:51.583 --> 00:35:54.542
Why are you hitting my servants like that?

572
00:35:55.583 --> 00:35:58.458
No one can recover their memories
if you keep hitting them.

573
00:35:58.958 --> 00:36:00.083
I read somewhere…

574
00:36:00.625 --> 00:36:01.833
because I read a lot…

575
00:36:02.833 --> 00:36:06.333
that people can regain their memories

576
00:36:06.875 --> 00:36:08.958
by repeating their past life actions.

577
00:36:09.292 --> 00:36:10.625
Like I just did!

578
00:36:11.250 --> 00:36:13.333
He's right.
Isn't that true, Uncle?

579
00:36:13.417 --> 00:36:15.217
Absolutely, 200% right!
Right, Brother-in-law?

580
00:36:16.042 --> 00:36:17.042
Alright, fine.

581
00:36:17.417 --> 00:36:18.417
Alright, fine.

582
00:36:18.500 --> 00:36:19.542
So it's settled!

583
00:36:20.042 --> 00:36:23.292
The three of you will stay
in our palace and serve us.

584
00:36:23.500 --> 00:36:26.667
We three will strangle you instead.

585
00:36:26.750 --> 00:36:29.250
We won't be able to find
the treasure unless you go there!

586
00:37:02.875 --> 00:37:05.000
<i>Hocus-pocus, whisper in every ear</i>

587
00:37:05.083 --> 00:37:07.208
<i>Who will play quietly here?</i>

588
00:37:07.292 --> 00:37:09.333
<i>With eyes closed tight</i>

589
00:37:09.417 --> 00:37:11.292
<i>I'll fill the world with sound</i>

590
00:37:11.375 --> 00:37:15.458
<i>Spinning fortune all around</i>

591
00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:18.125
<i>Hocus-pocus, whisper in every ear</i>

592
00:37:18.208 --> 00:37:20.292
<i>Sing that song again in Hindi, dear</i>

593
00:37:20.375 --> 00:37:22.458
<i>All the dust of the moon</i>

594
00:37:22.542 --> 00:37:24.333
<i>I'll gather and tie them up soon</i>

595
00:37:24.417 --> 00:37:28.792
<i>With a flick of my wrist
I'll make them vanish like mist</i>

596
00:37:53.042 --> 00:37:57.292
<i>From Baba's bag
A skeleton was found</i>

597
00:37:57.375 --> 00:38:01.667
<i>And "Oh my God!" echoed
In Bengal all around</i>

598
00:38:01.750 --> 00:38:05.583
<i>From Baba's bag
A skeleton was found</i>

599
00:38:06.167 --> 00:38:10.000
<i>And "Oh my God!" echoed
In Bengal all around</i>

600
00:38:10.375 --> 00:38:14.708
<i>Where he steps
There the doom may spread</i>

601
00:38:14.875 --> 00:38:19.125
<i>Chant God's name instead
And let faith be led</i>

602
00:38:19.208 --> 00:38:23.542
<i>Four times four makes sixteen
Divide it by four and four is seen</i>

603
00:38:23.625 --> 00:38:25.708
<i>Hocus-pocus, whisper in every ear</i>

604
00:38:25.792 --> 00:38:27.875
<i>Give me the right count, dear</i>

605
00:38:27.958 --> 00:38:30.000
<i>Four hundred eggs of eagles are revealed</i>

606
00:38:30.083 --> 00:38:31.917
<i>They're boiled and peeled</i>

607
00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:34.667
<i>With a flick of my wrist
I'll make them vanish like mist</i>

608
00:38:45.542 --> 00:38:48.750
<i>Glory to Goddess Durga!</i>

609
00:39:11.958 --> 00:39:15.417
<i>Glory to Goddess Durga!</i>

610
00:40:06.708 --> 00:40:07.708
Who are you?

611
00:40:12.167 --> 00:40:13.167
Mallika.

612
00:40:13.417 --> 00:40:15.333
I work for Crown Heritage Restoration.

613
00:40:16.208 --> 00:40:19.375
Oh, right! That's the company
that restores old properties.

614
00:40:19.542 --> 00:40:20.750
I had called them earlier.

615
00:40:21.792 --> 00:40:24.333
But weren't they sending Mr. Kaushik?

616
00:40:24.417 --> 00:40:25.917
He's on extended leave.

617
00:40:26.292 --> 00:40:27.542
Extended leave?

618
00:40:27.958 --> 00:40:29.838
I spoke to him just yesterday.
Give me a second.

619
00:40:36.542 --> 00:40:37.542
He's not answering.

620
00:40:37.750 --> 00:40:39.917
As I mentioned,
he's on an extended leave.

621
00:40:40.167 --> 00:40:43.083
It's alright. She's here in his place.

622
00:40:43.333 --> 00:40:44.333
Welcome!

623
00:40:44.750 --> 00:40:45.750
Welcome.

624
00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:54.280
So, you're the one who's reincarnated
as the Crown Prince?

625
00:40:54.875 --> 00:40:55.875
Yes.

626
00:40:56.625 --> 00:40:58.345
Have you started to regain
any memories yet?

627
00:40:58.875 --> 00:41:01.292
Like your father,
the king, other relatives,

628
00:41:01.542 --> 00:41:02.542
or your sister,

629
00:41:03.167 --> 00:41:04.167
Manjulika?

630
00:41:06.167 --> 00:41:07.792
Not yet.

631
00:41:09.542 --> 00:41:10.768
Don't worry, it will come back.

632
00:41:10.792 --> 00:41:12.125
Yeah, soon.

633
00:41:12.792 --> 00:41:14.312
Come with me. I'll show you your room.

634
00:42:13.125 --> 00:42:14.125
That was a close call!

635
00:42:30.583 --> 00:42:31.583
Put this here.

636
00:42:31.625 --> 00:42:32.826
This place has such bad vibes.

637
00:42:35.542 --> 00:42:36.542
Inception?!

638
00:42:38.542 --> 00:42:40.292
Meera. Don't jump again.

639
00:42:40.542 --> 00:42:42.000
There are stairs to go down.

640
00:42:43.083 --> 00:42:44.143
- I won't let you jump!
- Hey…

641
00:42:44.167 --> 00:42:45.000
I won't let you jump!

642
00:42:45.083 --> 00:42:46.476
- I won't let you fall!
- Move aside. Leave me.

643
00:42:46.500 --> 00:42:47.333
What are you doing?

644
00:42:47.417 --> 00:42:48.726
Are you looking for reasons to touch me?

645
00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:51.042
I thought you were going
to jump like you did last night.

646
00:42:51.583 --> 00:42:52.583
Last night?

647
00:42:52.750 --> 00:42:53.750
Where did I jump?

648
00:42:54.833 --> 00:42:55.875
In my dream.

649
00:42:56.542 --> 00:42:57.542
Oh,

650
00:42:57.917 --> 00:42:59.833
so you're dreaming about my death now?

651
00:42:59.917 --> 00:43:02.083
No one can control their dreams.

652
00:43:03.167 --> 00:43:04.958
If I could control mine,

653
00:43:06.208 --> 00:43:10.458
you cannot even imagine the dreams
I'd have about you.

654
00:43:14.708 --> 00:43:16.250
Who's looking for reasons
to touch now?

655
00:43:17.042 --> 00:43:17.875
Should I let go?

656
00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:19.000
No!

657
00:43:20.708 --> 00:43:21.708
That was a close call.

658
00:43:23.125 --> 00:43:24.542
You're such a pervert!

659
00:43:25.875 --> 00:43:26.875
No, I'm just a guy.

660
00:43:27.458 --> 00:43:28.458
Crazy fool.

661
00:43:31.417 --> 00:43:32.417
Crazy girl.

662
00:43:32.917 --> 00:43:34.417
Long live, revolution!

663
00:43:34.500 --> 00:43:36.333
Long live, revolution!

664
00:43:36.417 --> 00:43:40.500
- Everyone knows this…
- Our boss is a thief!

665
00:43:40.583 --> 00:43:42.083
- Everyone…
- Shut up, morons.

666
00:43:42.167 --> 00:43:44.583
We've been out here protesting
since morning.

667
00:43:44.667 --> 00:43:45.667
What's all this nonsense?

668
00:43:45.750 --> 00:43:49.500
You're messing up our lives
with your excuses.

669
00:43:49.583 --> 00:43:54.167
You had me clean a gutter
and messed up my future.

670
00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:56.292
I won't work for you anymore.

671
00:43:56.375 --> 00:43:57.917
I won't do it. That's it.

672
00:43:58.000 --> 00:44:00.875
And I'm not cooking for you at all.

673
00:44:00.958 --> 00:44:03.667
You're so cruel.

674
00:44:04.083 --> 00:44:05.500
You made me mop the floor.

675
00:44:05.667 --> 00:44:08.292
My hands are all blistered now.

676
00:44:08.375 --> 00:44:10.458
You should've told me sooner.

677
00:44:11.292 --> 00:44:14.625
We could've figured out another way
to get your memories back.

678
00:44:14.708 --> 00:44:16.458
So find one now!

679
00:44:16.542 --> 00:44:18.458
If I could find a hunter…

680
00:44:18.542 --> 00:44:20.083
By "hunter," do you mean a whip?

681
00:44:20.167 --> 00:44:22.208
The whip is in there.

682
00:44:23.042 --> 00:44:24.042
Why do you want a whip?

683
00:44:24.083 --> 00:44:26.625
In the past life,
whenever you made a mistake,

684
00:44:27.250 --> 00:44:28.792
I'd whip your faces.

685
00:44:29.250 --> 00:44:30.292
You'd whip our faces.

686
00:44:30.375 --> 00:44:31.833
Just around 250 whips,

687
00:44:32.375 --> 00:44:34.175
and you'll get your memories back
on your own.

688
00:44:39.583 --> 00:44:41.333
Done with 250 whips!

689
00:44:41.542 --> 00:44:42.708
Are you okay?

690
00:44:42.792 --> 00:44:43.833
I'm fine.

691
00:44:43.917 --> 00:44:47.000
What are you waiting
for with the phenol in the bucket? A fly?

692
00:44:47.375 --> 00:44:49.333
<i>Mop the floor</i>

693
00:44:49.417 --> 00:44:51.125
<i>Mop the floor</i>

694
00:44:51.208 --> 00:44:53.917
<i>Hey, bro!</i>

695
00:44:54.042 --> 00:44:56.667
<i>What do you want to eat today?</i>

696
00:44:56.792 --> 00:44:59.625
<i>Palak </i>paneer or paneer <i>pasanda</i>?

697
00:44:59.708 --> 00:45:00.708
Make both of them!

698
00:45:01.292 --> 00:45:03.167
I'll eat them and let you know
what I like.

699
00:45:03.250 --> 00:45:07.083
Run before he asks me
to make a third dish!

700
00:45:24.708 --> 00:45:25.908
You still haven't gone to bed?

701
00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:31.083
Careful! Be careful.

702
00:45:32.500 --> 00:45:35.083
All the weapons you see
here belonged to Manjulika.

703
00:45:36.875 --> 00:45:38.500
She loved weapons.

704
00:45:39.042 --> 00:45:41.500
No one around here
had a better aim than her.

705
00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:46.292
She wouldn't miss her target
even with her eyes closed.

706
00:45:51.708 --> 00:45:52.708
Like this?

707
00:45:56.917 --> 00:45:57.917
Come on, Ms. Mallika,

708
00:45:58.083 --> 00:46:00.083
do you really think
you're as good as Manjulika?

709
00:46:01.083 --> 00:46:04.583
Not everyone can hit
the target like she did.

710
00:46:06.917 --> 00:46:08.750
- Go to bed.
- Yes.

711
00:46:33.083 --> 00:46:34.083
Hello.

712
00:46:34.625 --> 00:46:35.917
Rooh Baba speaking.

713
00:46:54.042 --> 00:46:56.875
<i>I'd like to welcome our late-night
listeners once again.</i>

714
00:46:57.542 --> 00:47:00.042
<i>Let's talk to our next caller.</i>

715
00:47:05.667 --> 00:47:06.708
<i>What's your name?</i>

716
00:47:07.458 --> 00:47:09.333
<i>Manjulika.</i>

717
00:47:09.708 --> 00:47:11.583
<i>Who do you want to leave a message for?</i>

718
00:47:11.667 --> 00:47:13.667
<i>My brother.</i>

719
00:47:15.958 --> 00:47:17.792
<i>My precious.</i>

720
00:47:18.250 --> 00:47:19.750
<i>My darling brother.</i>

721
00:47:21.375 --> 00:47:23.000
<i>You are back,</i>

722
00:47:23.417 --> 00:47:25.125
<i>but you won't survive for long.</i>

723
00:47:26.708 --> 00:47:28.292
<i>I'm out now,</i>

724
00:47:28.833 --> 00:47:31.542
<i>and I'm very close to you.</i>

725
00:47:32.375 --> 00:47:35.667
<i>You are destined to die by my doing,
this time as well.</i>

726
00:47:36.125 --> 00:47:38.917
<i>You will meet the same fate as I did.</i>

727
00:47:39.375 --> 00:47:41.208
<i>I will burn you!</i>

728
00:47:41.542 --> 00:47:42.667
<i>You will burn!</i>

729
00:47:42.833 --> 00:47:43.875
Please.

730
00:47:44.167 --> 00:47:45.167
Sorry.

731
00:47:58.750 --> 00:48:00.042
<i>Clack bat!</i>

732
00:48:01.250 --> 00:48:02.083
Black cat!

733
00:48:02.208 --> 00:48:03.375
Scram! Go away!

734
00:48:04.708 --> 00:48:06.917
- Fire!
- Where's the fire?!

735
00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:08.583
Oh no!

736
00:48:08.833 --> 00:48:10.167
- It's on fire!
- It's on fire!

737
00:48:10.250 --> 00:48:11.500
Someone put it out!

738
00:48:11.583 --> 00:48:12.417
It's on fire!

739
00:48:12.500 --> 00:48:14.167
It's on fire!

740
00:48:14.250 --> 00:48:16.500
It's burning!

741
00:48:16.583 --> 00:48:19.042
- Someone put it out!
- It's burning!

742
00:48:37.042 --> 00:48:39.167
How did this painting burn by itself?

743
00:48:39.250 --> 00:48:43.667
What you really need to ask
is why <i>this </i>painting caught fire.

744
00:48:44.042 --> 00:48:46.667
- Manjulika must have done it.
- Yes.

745
00:48:46.750 --> 00:48:49.583
She had a feud with this Crown Prince.

746
00:48:49.667 --> 00:48:51.708
Enemy. I told you,

747
00:48:52.042 --> 00:48:53.792
we shouldn't have come here.

748
00:48:56.500 --> 00:48:57.958
Oh no!

749
00:48:58.583 --> 00:48:59.583
It's burnt.

750
00:48:59.708 --> 00:49:00.833
So sad!

751
00:49:02.958 --> 00:49:04.458
You look scared as if

752
00:49:04.792 --> 00:49:07.042
it's you that's on fire
and not the painting.

753
00:49:09.542 --> 00:49:11.042
It's just a painting.

754
00:49:23.833 --> 00:49:28.125
<i>O' Lord of the entire universe</i>

755
00:49:28.833 --> 00:49:29.833
<i>Mighty Lord of...</i>

756
00:49:29.875 --> 00:49:31.355
Stop it, Tillu. I'm not answering it.

757
00:49:32.375 --> 00:49:33.250
Hey, Tillu!

758
00:49:33.333 --> 00:49:34.833
Why aren't you answering my calls?

759
00:49:35.292 --> 00:49:36.559
And why did you change your ringtone?

760
00:49:36.583 --> 00:49:38.458
Manjulika is threatening me on the radio,

761
00:49:38.625 --> 00:49:40.976
and Prince Debendra Nath's
painting just spontaneously caught fire.

762
00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:42.000
And he's me.

763
00:49:42.042 --> 00:49:43.042
What?

764
00:49:43.500 --> 00:49:45.000
I'm someone important, Tillu.

765
00:49:45.750 --> 00:49:46.750
I'm royal.

766
00:49:47.083 --> 00:49:48.083
You don't know.

767
00:49:48.417 --> 00:49:50.583
I'm getting out of this maze,
and you should too.

768
00:49:50.667 --> 00:49:52.375
- Come on, let's go.
- Excuse me, hello!

769
00:49:52.667 --> 00:49:54.027
Don't even think about going back.

770
00:49:54.125 --> 00:49:55.525
I ran away from there to come here.

771
00:49:55.583 --> 00:49:56.917
- Ran away?
- Why?

772
00:49:57.000 --> 00:50:00.625
The client we cheated on turned out
to be ACP Rathore's brother.

773
00:50:00.792 --> 00:50:02.208
Who's ACP Rathore?

774
00:50:02.292 --> 00:50:03.542
How should I know?

775
00:50:03.750 --> 00:50:05.333
Isn't it enough that he's an ACP?

776
00:50:05.458 --> 00:50:06.750
I heard he's pretty dangerous.

777
00:50:06.833 --> 00:50:09.353
Anyone who ends up in his sights goes
to prison for a long time.

778
00:50:10.917 --> 00:50:12.000
Damn it.

779
00:50:12.083 --> 00:50:14.958
On one side, we have ACP Rathore,
and on the other, Manjulika.

780
00:50:15.417 --> 00:50:16.417
What should I do now?

781
00:50:17.208 --> 00:50:19.792
Let's get as far away as possible
and go underground,

782
00:50:19.875 --> 00:50:20.750
then we'll figure it out.

783
00:50:20.875 --> 00:50:24.667
But first, delete that video
from that witch's phone.

784
00:50:24.792 --> 00:50:25.792
Yes.

785
00:50:26.333 --> 00:50:27.167
Okay.

786
00:50:27.333 --> 00:50:29.208
And what were you saying about Manjulika?

787
00:50:29.583 --> 00:50:30.500
Who is she?

788
00:50:30.583 --> 00:50:31.958
She's a bloody witch!

789
00:50:32.292 --> 00:50:33.601
She's a ghost, a spirit, a vampire!

790
00:50:33.625 --> 00:50:35.083
She appears at the sight of blood!

791
00:50:49.583 --> 00:50:51.250
Hey, sweetie, come down!

792
00:50:51.708 --> 00:50:52.708
I said come down.

793
00:50:52.917 --> 00:50:53.917
Coming!

794
00:50:54.500 --> 00:50:55.500
What is it?

795
00:50:56.667 --> 00:50:58.125
- Can you do me a favor?
- Why?

796
00:50:59.375 --> 00:51:01.875
Listen, I need your sister's phone.

797
00:51:02.042 --> 00:51:03.333
But she can't find out about it.

798
00:51:03.750 --> 00:51:04.911
You'll help me, right, kiddo?

799
00:51:05.542 --> 00:51:06.417
Get lost!

800
00:51:06.500 --> 00:51:07.917
I'm of royal blood.

801
00:51:08.250 --> 00:51:09.750
And I'm always loyal.

802
00:51:10.208 --> 00:51:13.042
You want me to betray my own sister?

803
00:51:13.292 --> 00:51:14.292
I'll give you 20 bucks.

804
00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:18.250
Done!

805
00:51:21.042 --> 00:51:23.208
It wasn't blood, it was just sauce.

806
00:51:23.375 --> 00:51:25.042
- Are you sure?
- Did you get it, kiddo?

807
00:51:25.167 --> 00:51:26.167
Good job!

808
00:51:27.333 --> 00:51:29.214
- Password?
- You'll need to give me another 20.

809
00:51:31.667 --> 00:51:32.667
Enjoy your extra samosas.

810
00:51:35.292 --> 00:51:36.292
One-two-three-four.

811
00:52:04.917 --> 00:52:07.625
I knew you would try to steal my phone.

812
00:52:08.333 --> 00:52:10.083
Good thing I have it password protected.

813
00:52:11.333 --> 00:52:13.250
- You don't like me, right?
- What?

814
00:52:14.292 --> 00:52:15.292
Not at all!

815
00:52:15.750 --> 00:52:16.667
Why?

816
00:52:16.750 --> 00:52:19.125
Because you seem one way but act another.

817
00:52:19.833 --> 00:52:21.333
It's hard to figure you out.

818
00:52:22.125 --> 00:52:24.167
But I understand you perfectly.

819
00:52:24.292 --> 00:52:26.333
Excuse me, don't act smart.

820
00:52:26.417 --> 00:52:27.500
Just remember,

821
00:52:27.583 --> 00:52:31.417
you can't think about leaving as long as
I have that video on my phone.

822
00:52:32.083 --> 00:52:34.625
I look like a rascal
when I dress up as Rooh Baba.

823
00:52:34.917 --> 00:52:35.917
Don't you think?

824
00:52:41.375 --> 00:52:42.855
I can't say anything about the video,

825
00:52:43.667 --> 00:52:47.542
but I'm not going anywhere
while you have my photos on your phone.

826
00:53:17.375 --> 00:53:23.292
<i>There's been no one since you were gone</i>

827
00:53:23.375 --> 00:53:29.333
<i>This heart of mine feels
Like an empty ground</i>

828
00:53:29.417 --> 00:53:32.292
<i>With your dreams, I longed</i>

829
00:53:32.375 --> 00:53:38.125
<i>In that same place</i>

830
00:53:38.417 --> 00:53:41.250
<i>I waited for so long</i>

831
00:53:41.333 --> 00:53:47.292
<i>So subtly, without a sign, or clue</i>

832
00:53:47.375 --> 00:53:53.333
<i>I fell in love with you deeper than I knew</i>

833
00:53:53.417 --> 00:53:59.292
<i>So subtly, without a sign, or a clue</i>

834
00:53:59.375 --> 00:54:06.167
<i>I fell in love with you deeper than I knew</i>

835
00:54:20.375 --> 00:54:26.250
<i>What we shared</i>

836
00:54:26.792 --> 00:54:31.583
<i>Was it real or just a game?</i>

837
00:54:32.417 --> 00:54:35.333
<i>Was it love</i>

838
00:54:35.417 --> 00:54:42.417
<i>Or just a fleeting flame?</i>

839
00:54:44.333 --> 00:54:49.958
<i>My life is yours, just say the word</i>

840
00:54:50.375 --> 00:54:57.375
<i>Ask, and all will be conferred</i>

841
00:54:59.292 --> 00:55:02.292
<i>I can't bear this solitude's weight</i>

842
00:55:02.375 --> 00:55:05.292
<i>I can't escape her memories even today</i>

843
00:55:05.375 --> 00:55:08.250
<i>I made her my shadow, my bae</i>

844
00:55:08.333 --> 00:55:11.333
<i>She was close to me yet so far away</i>

845
00:55:11.417 --> 00:55:17.250
<i>So subtly, without a sign, or a clue</i>

846
00:55:17.333 --> 00:55:23.917
<i>I fell in love with you deeper than I knew</i>

847
00:55:40.417 --> 00:55:41.875
Who is this woman in the painting?

848
00:55:42.625 --> 00:55:43.625
Madhulika Devi.

849
00:55:43.708 --> 00:55:44.708
Manjulika?

850
00:55:45.042 --> 00:55:46.667
No, it's Madhulika Devi!

851
00:55:47.458 --> 00:55:49.208
Prince Debendra Nath's wife.

852
00:55:50.125 --> 00:55:51.125
Oh, so she's my wife!

853
00:55:51.833 --> 00:55:52.833
She's quite hot.

854
00:55:57.167 --> 00:56:01.250
But her chin looks a lot like yours.

855
00:56:02.292 --> 00:56:03.375
Are you…

856
00:56:03.667 --> 00:56:05.250
Do you always have to act like this?

857
00:56:05.417 --> 00:56:07.375
I said you're hot too,
but you didn't catch that.

858
00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:09.000
Listen.

859
00:56:09.833 --> 00:56:11.458
I really don't want to hear it.
Just go.

860
00:56:11.625 --> 00:56:13.750
Where should I go?
That's Manjulika's room...

861
00:56:21.042 --> 00:56:22.083
This is here.

862
00:56:22.333 --> 00:56:23.814
But it was supposed to go over there.

863
00:56:24.167 --> 00:56:25.542
- This…
- The protective shield…

864
00:56:33.417 --> 00:56:34.417
Leave this palace!

865
00:56:38.250 --> 00:56:39.250
I won't spare you!

866
00:56:40.833 --> 00:56:42.042
You will die.

867
00:56:59.542 --> 00:57:01.583
Leave this palace!

868
00:57:34.375 --> 00:57:35.458
Run!

869
00:57:35.542 --> 00:57:36.542
Let me go!

870
00:57:37.792 --> 00:57:38.792
Run!

871
00:57:52.000 --> 00:57:53.000
Let go of my hand.

872
00:57:55.792 --> 00:57:56.792
What are you doing?

873
00:57:57.625 --> 00:57:58.625
Let me go.

874
00:58:03.333 --> 00:58:04.333
Where are you taking me?

875
00:58:04.417 --> 00:58:05.625
Manjulika's in there.

876
00:58:06.208 --> 00:58:07.208
Go away!

877
00:58:08.667 --> 00:58:09.750
I told you to leave!

878
00:58:09.833 --> 00:58:11.713
But you have brought
someone else along instead.

879
00:58:12.583 --> 00:58:13.583
Leave!

880
00:58:13.958 --> 00:58:15.542
Why won't you leave?

881
00:58:15.625 --> 00:58:16.917
Leave!

882
00:58:17.083 --> 00:58:19.042
My throat's hurting!

883
00:58:19.125 --> 00:58:21.708
Please go away.

884
00:58:22.375 --> 00:58:25.750
You've hurt me, my precious.

885
00:58:26.583 --> 00:58:28.083
My precious? It's you.

886
00:58:28.375 --> 00:58:30.708
And me too.

887
00:58:30.833 --> 00:58:32.750
You've hurt my sister-in-law!

888
00:58:32.833 --> 00:58:34.518
So you three have been trying
to scare me all this time?

889
00:58:34.542 --> 00:58:36.750
We weren't trying to scare you,
we were scared as well.

890
00:58:37.125 --> 00:58:40.875
You were here to take this lovely,
well-decorated house!

891
00:58:40.958 --> 00:58:42.250
Drama queens,

892
00:58:42.792 --> 00:58:44.042
how long have you been here?

893
00:58:44.125 --> 00:58:45.583
Let's sit down and discuss this.

894
00:58:46.208 --> 00:58:48.049
- When did your mother die?
- When did she die?

895
00:58:48.208 --> 00:58:49.208
Two years ago.

896
00:58:49.458 --> 00:58:50.458
Two years.

897
00:58:50.750 --> 00:58:51.583
Two years!

898
00:58:51.667 --> 00:58:55.833
Sister, we're really just imposters
from Haldighati.

899
00:58:56.083 --> 00:58:58.333
We change our looks to fit in.

900
00:58:58.417 --> 00:58:59.625
Like chameleons.

901
00:59:00.125 --> 00:59:03.208
We showed up here two years ago
in our Rolls Royce.

902
00:59:03.625 --> 00:59:04.458
Rolls Royce?

903
00:59:04.542 --> 00:59:06.417
Yeah, our two buffaloes!

904
00:59:06.708 --> 00:59:08.833
<i>One's named Rolls,
and the other is Royce.</i>

905
00:59:08.917 --> 00:59:10.917
ROLLS ROYCE

906
00:59:11.000 --> 00:59:13.750
<i>Our village experienced a flood.</i>

907
00:59:14.000 --> 00:59:15.500
<i>We left for Japan.</i>

908
00:59:15.583 --> 00:59:17.583
<i>We got stuck here because of the storm.</i>

909
00:59:17.833 --> 00:59:21.708
<i>We came into the palace
to escape the storm.</i>

910
00:59:33.458 --> 00:59:34.750
Oh, my God!

911
00:59:34.917 --> 00:59:35.917
What do you see?

912
00:59:36.417 --> 00:59:38.417
This is Manjulika's palace.

913
00:59:38.500 --> 00:59:39.625
Who's Manjulika?

914
00:59:39.958 --> 00:59:42.500
The famous witch of this village.

915
00:59:42.583 --> 00:59:44.917
Oh!

916
00:59:45.125 --> 00:59:47.875
<i>I am yours</i>

917
00:59:50.125 --> 00:59:51.125
Where are you going?

918
00:59:51.625 --> 00:59:53.145
What if that witch grabs you in there?

919
00:59:53.667 --> 00:59:56.792
So? I've been with you for 35 years.

920
00:59:57.625 --> 00:59:59.625
What could that witch possibly do to me?

921
01:00:00.417 --> 01:00:01.958
And even if she does,

922
01:00:02.333 --> 01:00:03.833
I'm sure to like it.

923
01:00:06.083 --> 01:00:07.417
But how did the lock break?

924
01:00:07.500 --> 01:00:09.417
Oh my God, that lock…

925
01:00:10.042 --> 01:00:15.375
Her bald Raj Purohit's ancestor put
in a lock that was heavier than he was!

926
01:00:15.750 --> 01:00:19.083
It probably rusted over time
and just fell off.

927
01:00:19.417 --> 01:00:20.250
And Manjulika?

928
01:00:20.333 --> 01:00:21.375
<i>When we arrived,</i>

929
01:00:21.625 --> 01:00:23.333
<i>Manjulika wasn't here.</i>

930
01:00:24.542 --> 01:00:27.042
Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal for Mumtaz,

931
01:00:27.125 --> 01:00:30.875
and Manjulika created this
"home sweet home" for us.

932
01:00:30.958 --> 01:00:36.833
<i>Everyone here is just having a good time
Under the pretext of love</i>

933
01:00:37.833 --> 01:00:40.417
<i>To keep Manjulika's legend and fear alive,</i>

934
01:00:40.625 --> 01:00:43.250
<i>I locked the door
with a lock larger than myself.</i>

935
01:00:44.167 --> 01:00:48.708
<i>So that no lost souls like us
could come in.</i>

936
01:00:50.250 --> 01:00:52.958
Then you showed up
and messed up our fun.

937
01:00:53.125 --> 01:00:56.625
We would've been done if you had opened
the door on Durga Ashtami.

938
01:00:56.708 --> 01:00:58.667
- Right.
- Oh, my God,

939
01:00:58.833 --> 01:01:01.750
we worked so hard to get rid of him!

940
01:01:07.333 --> 01:01:09.833
Just like in an Alfred Hitchcock movie.

941
01:01:10.125 --> 01:01:11.583
Keep scaring him like that!

942
01:01:11.667 --> 01:01:12.667
Yes!

943
01:01:15.625 --> 01:01:16.865
What have I gotten myself into?

944
01:01:17.667 --> 01:01:20.708
My eyes did the trick!

945
01:01:21.167 --> 01:01:22.083
Was he scared?

946
01:01:22.167 --> 01:01:24.500
He was super scared!
Totally freaked out!

947
01:01:27.917 --> 01:01:29.042
Rooh Baba,

948
01:01:29.708 --> 01:01:31.829
I'm going to give you an out-of-body
experience today.

949
01:01:32.417 --> 01:01:33.417
Very good.

950
01:01:33.500 --> 01:01:34.958
Fire!

951
01:01:35.042 --> 01:01:36.625
Fire!

952
01:01:36.792 --> 01:01:39.708
But you turned out
to be really hard to scare.

953
01:01:39.792 --> 01:01:41.583
You even got me slapped!

954
01:01:43.750 --> 01:01:44.792
Sister Mallika,

955
01:01:46.708 --> 01:01:49.333
how did you know
it was me trying to scare you?

956
01:01:50.333 --> 01:01:52.667
Because I know you are not Manjulika.

957
01:01:53.875 --> 01:01:56.042
Oh no, she recognized us.

958
01:01:56.542 --> 01:01:57.542
Yes.

959
01:01:58.125 --> 01:01:59.125
Well,

960
01:01:59.500 --> 01:02:02.060
now that we've told you the whole story
and explained everything,

961
01:02:02.375 --> 01:02:03.917
it's time for us to sleep.

962
01:02:04.417 --> 01:02:06.042
You should leave our home.

963
01:02:06.208 --> 01:02:07.208
Good night.

964
01:02:07.583 --> 01:02:10.250
Forget good night…
I'll make you say goodbye!

965
01:02:10.333 --> 01:02:12.333
- I'll get you for this!
- We'll leave…

966
01:02:12.417 --> 01:02:16.000
You dressed up as a ghost and tried
to scare me, you shameless people!

967
01:02:16.875 --> 01:02:17.708
I'm going to tell my father

968
01:02:17.792 --> 01:02:19.512
- about you right now.
- Where are you going?

969
01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:21.684
Why are you ruining my chance
to get ten million?

970
01:02:21.708 --> 01:02:23.042
You love me, right?

971
01:02:24.042 --> 01:02:28.042
We'll tell your father, your uncle,
and the whole village tomorrow,

972
01:02:28.375 --> 01:02:29.500
but we'll do it in my way.

973
01:02:31.292 --> 01:02:32.292
Okay.

974
01:02:33.042 --> 01:02:36.833
Mallika, you exposed them
and solved all our problems.

975
01:02:38.000 --> 01:02:39.875
It's the least I could do for you.

976
01:02:40.583 --> 01:02:42.542
After all, you're like
a little brother to me.

977
01:02:44.167 --> 01:02:45.958
So, can you do me another favor?

978
01:02:46.417 --> 01:02:47.417
What's that?

979
01:02:48.375 --> 01:02:52.458
Can you be Manjulika
for a little while tomorrow?

980
01:02:53.750 --> 01:02:54.750
Me?

981
01:02:55.583 --> 01:02:56.583
Manjulika?

982
01:03:03.750 --> 01:03:04.750
What's wrong?

983
01:03:05.083 --> 01:03:06.083
Nothing.

984
01:03:06.958 --> 01:03:07.958
I'll do it.

985
01:03:09.583 --> 01:03:10.417
Thank you.

986
01:03:10.542 --> 01:03:11.542
Let's go.

987
01:03:19.792 --> 01:03:20.917
Villagers,

988
01:03:21.625 --> 01:03:25.417
I really thought I should wait until
Durga Ashtami to open this door.

989
01:03:26.458 --> 01:03:28.958
But you've all been waiting for 200 years!

990
01:03:29.167 --> 01:03:30.647
So why should we waste any more time?

991
01:03:31.167 --> 01:03:33.042
That's why I'm opening this door today

992
01:03:33.583 --> 01:03:36.583
to finally close the chapter on Manjulika.

993
01:03:36.958 --> 01:03:39.792
- Raj Purohit clearly said…
- Calm down, sir.

994
01:03:40.583 --> 01:03:42.792
I know it's a tough task.

995
01:03:43.125 --> 01:03:45.125
That's why to help me with this task

996
01:03:45.625 --> 01:03:47.266
I've got this village's these
three great…

997
01:03:47.667 --> 01:03:48.500
pundits!

998
01:03:48.583 --> 01:03:50.351
- Wonderful!
- Let's give them a big round of applause!

999
01:03:50.375 --> 01:03:52.625
Come on up here, Pundit.
Don't be shy.

1000
01:03:52.708 --> 01:03:55.833
- Step forward! Come on.
- Greetings.

1001
01:03:55.917 --> 01:03:56.917
- Come on.
- Let's go.

1002
01:03:56.958 --> 01:03:59.083
- Welcome, welcome!
- Thank you.

1003
01:03:59.167 --> 01:04:00.167
Not over there.

1004
01:04:00.250 --> 01:04:01.708
Give me some respect.

1005
01:04:02.208 --> 01:04:04.083
While I do the rituals,

1006
01:04:04.292 --> 01:04:08.208
the Senior Pundit will walk
on burning coals and meditate. Well done!

1007
01:04:08.292 --> 01:04:09.167
- What?
- Yes!

1008
01:04:09.250 --> 01:04:13.250
And the Junior Pundit
will sit on an ice slab and meditate.

1009
01:04:13.417 --> 01:04:15.083
And you, Mrs. Pundit,

1010
01:04:15.208 --> 01:04:18.500
will roll around on the floor
and go around the area.

1011
01:04:18.583 --> 01:04:19.667
Oh no!

1012
01:04:19.750 --> 01:04:23.833
- Basanti, don't dance for them!
- I won't do it! I won't!

1013
01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:25.000
You won't do it?

1014
01:04:26.042 --> 01:04:28.667
You cheap con artists from Haldighati,

1015
01:04:28.875 --> 01:04:30.750
should I expose who you really are?

1016
01:04:31.625 --> 01:04:33.500
Why do you want to ruin our lives?

1017
01:04:33.583 --> 01:04:35.667
Glory to Senior Pundit!

1018
01:04:35.750 --> 01:04:37.958
Glory to Junior Pundit!

1019
01:04:38.042 --> 01:04:40.667
- Long live…
- Mrs. Pundit!

1020
01:04:44.042 --> 01:04:45.417
Come on, let's get started.

1021
01:04:45.583 --> 01:04:48.000
Come on, sit on the ice slab.

1022
01:04:48.708 --> 01:04:50.167
- I hate you!
- Hate you too.

1023
01:04:50.250 --> 01:04:51.250
Come on. Hurry up!

1024
01:04:53.625 --> 01:04:54.708
In the water…

1025
01:05:04.042 --> 01:05:05.042
Hurry up.

1026
01:05:08.875 --> 01:05:11.917
You're already eating the offerings
before the ritual starts!

1027
01:05:12.000 --> 01:05:13.768
Are you going to light the fire
with your eyes?

1028
01:05:13.792 --> 01:05:14.875
I can't find the matchbox.

1029
01:05:15.375 --> 01:05:16.833
Does anyone have a matchbox?

1030
01:05:17.292 --> 01:05:18.292
Matchbox, anyone?

1031
01:05:18.750 --> 01:05:20.167
<i>I have a lot of fire in me!</i>

1032
01:05:20.792 --> 01:05:22.000
Use this to light it.

1033
01:05:22.125 --> 01:05:23.125
Catch!

1034
01:05:37.125 --> 01:05:38.750
It's all an act.

1035
01:05:43.250 --> 01:05:44.250
Mummy!

1036
01:05:46.167 --> 01:05:48.792
Manjulika is going to die.

1037
01:05:51.542 --> 01:05:52.458
That's it.

1038
01:05:52.542 --> 01:05:53.542
Manjulika,

1039
01:05:54.250 --> 01:05:55.500
your game is over now.

1040
01:06:05.833 --> 01:06:06.833
Wait.

1041
01:06:12.667 --> 01:06:13.667
Stop!

1042
01:06:15.417 --> 01:06:16.737
It's dangerous to go any further.

1043
01:06:19.917 --> 01:06:22.625
Manju, I'm coming for you.

1044
01:06:23.208 --> 01:06:24.917
I just hope she does her part well.

1045
01:06:25.208 --> 01:06:26.375
Ms. Mallika, action!

1046
01:06:27.042 --> 01:06:28.958
Manjulika, come on out.

1047
01:06:32.167 --> 01:06:34.583
You've been hiding behind
that door for so long.

1048
01:06:35.083 --> 01:06:36.625
Do you want me to talk in Bengali?

1049
01:06:40.625 --> 01:06:42.042
Why so quiet, Manju?

1050
01:06:42.208 --> 01:06:43.250
Are you scared?

1051
01:06:43.500 --> 01:06:46.167
You think you can scare me?

1052
01:06:48.208 --> 01:06:49.958
You really think you can scare me?!

1053
01:06:52.042 --> 01:06:54.458
You don't know the fire
I have in my heart.

1054
01:06:55.250 --> 01:06:59.167
I'll burn you
and the whole family in this fire.

1055
01:07:02.333 --> 01:07:06.000
When that fire turns your body to ashes…

1056
01:07:06.250 --> 01:07:10.292
- My body?
- When your skin melts off your bones,

1057
01:07:10.750 --> 01:07:13.958
that's when I'll find peace.

1058
01:07:14.042 --> 01:07:17.042
I won't spare anyone! I'll kill you all!

1059
01:07:17.333 --> 01:07:20.417
I'll burn everything down!

1060
01:07:20.500 --> 01:07:21.583
Understood?

1061
01:07:21.667 --> 01:07:23.083
I won't spare anyone!

1062
01:07:23.167 --> 01:07:25.250
No one will be spared!

1063
01:07:25.458 --> 01:07:27.500
No one will be spared!

1064
01:07:57.125 --> 01:07:58.708
I drove Manjulika away!

1065
01:08:01.333 --> 01:08:03.250
I made her run away!

1066
01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:07.292
Glory to the Crown Prince!

1067
01:08:07.375 --> 01:08:09.208
Glory to the Crown Prince!

1068
01:08:09.292 --> 01:08:11.542
- Glory to the Crown Prince!
- Thank you.

1069
01:08:11.625 --> 01:08:13.667
Glory to the Crown Prince!

1070
01:08:16.833 --> 01:08:17.833
I warned you

1071
01:08:18.167 --> 01:08:20.083
not to open this door
before Durga Ashtami.

1072
01:08:21.458 --> 01:08:24.292
Look, Raj Purohit, I respect you a lot,

1073
01:08:24.542 --> 01:08:25.875
so I won't hide anything.

1074
01:08:26.667 --> 01:08:29.500
The truth is, Manjulika's story is a lie.

1075
01:08:29.708 --> 01:08:32.542
The pundits of this village
made it all up.

1076
01:08:32.917 --> 01:08:34.208
The door was already open.

1077
01:08:37.708 --> 01:08:38.708
What do you mean?

1078
01:08:40.125 --> 01:08:41.625
So Manjulika is already out?!

1079
01:08:43.792 --> 01:08:45.232
She's been waiting for someone then.

1080
01:08:46.167 --> 01:08:47.167
Who?

1081
01:08:49.458 --> 01:08:50.458
Maybe you.

1082
01:08:52.750 --> 01:08:54.042
<i>I can feel her presence,</i>

1083
01:08:54.333 --> 01:08:55.708
<i>she's close.</i>

1084
01:08:56.167 --> 01:08:57.917
<i>And she's about to make her next move.</i>

1085
01:09:30.292 --> 01:09:31.292
What is it?

1086
01:09:32.375 --> 01:09:33.875
It looks like a secret passage.

1087
01:09:34.625 --> 01:09:36.083
Let's see what secrets it hides.

1088
01:09:37.333 --> 01:09:38.708
Looks like a secret passage.

1089
01:10:02.125 --> 01:10:03.125
Strange,

1090
01:10:03.792 --> 01:10:05.667
one door opens,
and we find another locked one.

1091
01:10:06.458 --> 01:10:08.958
This feels more like a maze than a palace.

1092
01:10:09.250 --> 01:10:10.583
Raj Purohit?

1093
01:10:11.167 --> 01:10:12.167
What's going on?

1094
01:10:14.125 --> 01:10:15.708
I don't have an answer right now.

1095
01:10:18.042 --> 01:10:21.250
I need to go to the library established
by the Maharaja,

1096
01:10:21.333 --> 01:10:24.167
where the entire history of the royal
lineage is compiled and stored.

1097
01:10:26.083 --> 01:10:27.417
The answer will be found there.

1098
01:10:28.042 --> 01:10:29.125
But remember,

1099
01:10:30.917 --> 01:10:34.208
don't even think about opening
this door until Durga Ashtami.

1100
01:10:37.542 --> 01:10:38.542
Let's go.

1101
01:10:50.458 --> 01:10:52.179
Of course, Your Highness,
you can come here.

1102
01:10:52.208 --> 01:10:53.208
Welcome.

1103
01:10:54.458 --> 01:10:57.500
The whole market seems eager
to buy my palace now.

1104
01:10:58.625 --> 01:11:00.292
But that second door…

1105
01:11:01.000 --> 01:11:02.250
Everyone is going to run away.

1106
01:11:03.042 --> 01:11:04.042
Yes.

1107
01:11:04.083 --> 01:11:05.667
But we can't open that door.

1108
01:11:06.167 --> 01:11:07.958
Raj Purohit has ordered us not to.

1109
01:11:08.458 --> 01:11:09.498
Let's go, Tillu. Hurry up.

1110
01:11:09.542 --> 01:11:10.851
We need to catch the train
that leaves at ten.

1111
01:11:10.875 --> 01:11:11.750
Come on, let's move!

1112
01:11:11.833 --> 01:11:14.333
But why are you two leaving?

1113
01:11:16.042 --> 01:11:17.875
Because I can't stay in the dark anymore.

1114
01:11:19.125 --> 01:11:20.125
In the dark?

1115
01:11:20.292 --> 01:11:21.333
These lights are on now,

1116
01:11:22.500 --> 01:11:23.820
but they're going to go out soon.

1117
01:11:24.208 --> 01:11:25.569
You won't be able to pay the bill.

1118
01:11:25.833 --> 01:11:30.125
And no one will lend you money once
they find out about the second door.

1119
01:11:30.458 --> 01:11:33.583
And what if those who already
lent you money come to collect?

1120
01:11:33.917 --> 01:11:35.208
How will you repay them?

1121
01:11:36.375 --> 01:11:39.250
Uncle has sold his blood
so many times that he's run dry.

1122
01:11:39.750 --> 01:11:41.542
He'll sell his blood.

1123
01:11:41.708 --> 01:11:42.917
How can he?

1124
01:11:43.833 --> 01:11:45.583
The King doesn't have any left!

1125
01:11:45.833 --> 01:11:47.593
He's no king!
How can you even call him that?

1126
01:11:47.667 --> 01:11:49.292
He's poorer than we are!

1127
01:11:49.375 --> 01:11:51.136
Where are your manners,
you despicable being?

1128
01:11:51.542 --> 01:11:53.500
He might become even poorer,

1129
01:11:53.917 --> 01:11:55.792
and go back to the cattle shed,

1130
01:11:55.875 --> 01:11:57.708
and eat the bare minimum royal feast.

1131
01:11:57.833 --> 01:12:00.875
He might even use the toothpaste
I gave them for five years,

1132
01:12:00.958 --> 01:12:04.333
but don't forget he is a king!

1133
01:12:05.250 --> 01:12:07.500
You have so much respect for me.

1134
01:12:08.417 --> 01:12:09.833
Then why don't you help me?

1135
01:12:10.042 --> 01:12:11.583
We'd help you, Your Highness.

1136
01:12:11.917 --> 01:12:16.083
- You don't know the terror of Rooh Baba!
- Terror?

1137
01:12:16.292 --> 01:12:17.833
What can I say, Your Highness?

1138
01:12:19.208 --> 01:12:20.625
If I pass through a graveyard,

1139
01:12:20.708 --> 01:12:23.250
even the scariest ghosts,
spirits, witches, and souls

1140
01:12:23.500 --> 01:12:25.958
touch my feet and run away!

1141
01:12:26.958 --> 01:12:31.708
In villages up to 50 miles away,
witches tell their kids,

1142
01:12:31.792 --> 01:12:35.083
"Go to sleep, little witches,
or Rooh Baba will come!"

1143
01:12:35.708 --> 01:12:37.792
But we can't open the second door

1144
01:12:37.875 --> 01:12:40.000
because Raj Purohit ordered us not to!

1145
01:12:40.250 --> 01:12:43.875
He didn't even know about that door!

1146
01:12:44.917 --> 01:12:46.750
I can't live in poverty anymore.

1147
01:12:47.375 --> 01:12:49.875
Open the door,
consequences be damned.

1148
01:12:50.250 --> 01:12:51.750
As you wish, Your Highness.

1149
01:12:52.125 --> 01:12:54.042
Tillu, go call Meera and Uncle.

1150
01:12:54.125 --> 01:12:55.167
- Go.
- Perfect!

1151
01:14:30.250 --> 01:14:31.250
See?

1152
01:14:32.625 --> 01:14:33.625
I told you…

1153
01:14:34.667 --> 01:14:36.547
- there's nothing in here.
- What have you done?!

1154
01:14:36.583 --> 01:14:37.958
I just opened the door!

1155
01:14:38.083 --> 01:14:39.083
What have you done?

1156
01:14:39.792 --> 01:14:40.792
Disaster!

1157
01:14:42.042 --> 01:14:43.042
Utter disaster!

1158
01:14:44.417 --> 01:14:45.667
In that library,

1159
01:14:45.792 --> 01:14:48.750
I found something nobody knew about.

1160
01:14:49.583 --> 01:14:50.667
The Maharaja had not one,

1161
01:14:51.500 --> 01:14:52.583
but two daughters.

1162
01:14:53.583 --> 01:14:54.750
Princess Anjulika…

1163
01:14:55.625 --> 01:14:57.083
and Princess Manjulika.

1164
01:15:08.333 --> 01:15:09.917
If the younger sister was a storm,

1165
01:15:11.125 --> 01:15:13.708
the elder sister was a hurricane.

1166
01:15:22.333 --> 01:15:24.792
If one sister attacks from the shadows,

1167
01:15:25.750 --> 01:15:26.750
the other…

1168
01:15:28.250 --> 01:15:29.570
confronts with an open challenge.

1169
01:15:44.208 --> 01:15:46.750
Now that this door is open,
I can say with certainty

1170
01:15:47.500 --> 01:15:49.917
that annihilation is imminent.

1171
01:15:50.250 --> 01:15:54.000
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram</i>

1172
01:15:54.542 --> 01:15:58.542
<i>Hare Krishna Hare Ram</i>

1173
01:15:58.625 --> 01:16:00.583
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram</i>

1174
01:16:00.667 --> 01:16:02.542
<i>Hare Krishna Hare Ram</i>

1175
01:16:02.625 --> 01:16:04.708
<i>Hare Ram Hare Ram</i>

1176
01:16:04.833 --> 01:16:07.792
<i>Hare Krishna Hare Krishna Hare Krishna</i>

1177
01:16:07.875 --> 01:16:11.792
<i>Hare Krishna Hare Krishna Hare Ram</i>

1178
01:16:25.833 --> 01:16:29.333
Welcome to the court
of Shubhroto Maharaja,

1179
01:16:29.417 --> 01:16:32.042
the guardian of Rakhtghat.

1180
01:16:32.458 --> 01:16:34.750
Today, on this auspicious occasion
of Mohalaya,

1181
01:16:34.875 --> 01:16:38.083
showcasing their dance artistry…

1182
01:16:38.250 --> 01:16:42.125
we are delighted to present
Princess Manjulika and Princess Anjulika!

1183
01:17:30.542 --> 01:17:32.083
<i>Without you here</i>

1184
01:17:32.167 --> 01:17:39.167
<i>My heart's a wasteland</i>

1185
01:17:39.500 --> 01:17:46.500
<i>I'm like dry sand
You're the rain that's so grand</i>

1186
01:17:47.250 --> 01:17:48.792
<i>Without you here</i>

1187
01:17:48.875 --> 01:17:55.458
<i>My heart's a wasteland</i>

1188
01:17:56.167 --> 01:18:03.167
<i>I'm like dry sand
You're the rain that's so grand</i>

1189
01:18:03.583 --> 01:18:07.708
<i>My silent eyes ache with a sigh</i>

1190
01:18:07.792 --> 01:18:11.958
<i>I bow my head and send a prayer high</i>

1191
01:18:12.042 --> 01:18:16.125
<i>What is my life but a gift for you?</i>

1192
01:18:16.208 --> 01:18:18.208
<i>It can't be quenched
No matter what I do</i>

1193
01:18:18.292 --> 01:18:20.333
<i>This fire of eternal love
Burns bright and true</i>

1194
01:18:20.417 --> 01:18:25.458
<i>Oh, my beloved!</i>

1195
01:18:25.542 --> 01:18:29.083
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

1196
01:18:29.667 --> 01:18:33.875
<i>To this sweet tune of love's enthrall</i>

1197
01:18:33.958 --> 01:18:37.375
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

1198
01:18:38.042 --> 01:18:41.958
<i>My wishes</i>

1199
01:18:42.167 --> 01:18:46.042
<i>Will drift through the air</i>

1200
01:18:46.417 --> 01:18:50.500
<i>It will endure</i>

1201
01:18:50.583 --> 01:18:53.667
<i>Even in ruin</i>

1202
01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:04.833
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

1203
01:19:05.167 --> 01:19:09.333
<i>To this sweet tune of love's enthrall</i>

1204
01:19:09.417 --> 01:19:12.875
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

1205
01:19:13.458 --> 01:19:17.375
<i>My wishes</i>

1206
01:19:17.667 --> 01:19:21.500
<i>Will drift through the air</i>

1207
01:19:21.833 --> 01:19:28.750
<i>It will endure, even in ruin</i>

1208
01:19:36.542 --> 01:19:40.292
<i>I am yours</i>

1209
01:19:40.625 --> 01:19:44.458
<i>I am solely yours</i>

1210
01:19:44.875 --> 01:19:46.750
<i>I am yours</i>

1211
01:20:49.792 --> 01:20:53.208
<i>I am yours</i>

1212
01:20:53.292 --> 01:20:55.167
Excellent, truly excellent.

1213
01:20:56.083 --> 01:21:01.000
Impressed by your art,
I wish to give you both a gift.

1214
01:21:01.708 --> 01:21:05.833
I declare that on the auspicious
occasion of Durga Ashtami,

1215
01:21:05.917 --> 01:21:10.417
I will hand over the throne
to the new heir.

1216
01:21:10.500 --> 01:21:14.167
Glory to the Maharaja!

1217
01:21:14.250 --> 01:21:18.500
And that heir is
your younger brother,

1218
01:21:19.042 --> 01:21:20.708
my noble son,

1219
01:21:22.292 --> 01:21:24.333
Prince Debendra Nath!

1220
01:21:24.417 --> 01:21:26.333
Glory to the Maharaja!

1221
01:21:26.750 --> 01:21:29.250
Long live the Maharaja!

1222
01:21:29.500 --> 01:21:31.583
Glory to the Maharaja!

1223
01:21:32.000 --> 01:21:34.542
Glory to the Maharaja!

1224
01:21:34.792 --> 01:21:36.917
Glory to the Maharaja!

1225
01:21:37.583 --> 01:21:39.833
Glory to the Maharaja!

1226
01:22:01.708 --> 01:22:04.125
We've found two doors,
uncovered two sisters,

1227
01:22:04.208 --> 01:22:06.088
and these two are just sitting
here watching TV.

1228
01:22:34.167 --> 01:22:35.167
Is that…

1229
01:22:46.292 --> 01:22:47.833
Look behind you.

1230
01:22:50.208 --> 01:22:51.208
Look behind you.

1231
01:22:54.042 --> 01:22:55.958
Look behind you now!

1232
01:22:59.708 --> 01:23:00.708
Oh, you got scared!

1233
01:23:02.167 --> 01:23:03.167
Your Highness.

1234
01:23:05.458 --> 01:23:07.750
This is the Queen of Suryagarh,
Mandira Devi.

1235
01:23:07.917 --> 01:23:09.667
She wishes to purchase my palace.

1236
01:23:10.375 --> 01:23:12.083
I was really eager to meet you.

1237
01:23:12.750 --> 01:23:13.750
Eager?

1238
01:23:13.875 --> 01:23:16.000
I wanted to say "thank you" to you.

1239
01:23:16.375 --> 01:23:17.375
Thank you?

1240
01:23:17.792 --> 01:23:18.875
- To me?
- Yes.

1241
01:23:19.875 --> 01:23:21.667
I wouldn't have been able to come here

1242
01:23:22.708 --> 01:23:23.958
if you hadn't opened that door.

1243
01:23:24.917 --> 01:23:25.750
What do you mean?

1244
01:23:25.917 --> 01:23:27.500
I mean you opened that door

1245
01:23:27.958 --> 01:23:29.417
and got rid of Manjulika,

1246
01:23:29.708 --> 01:23:31.429
allowing me to come here
to buy this palace.

1247
01:23:32.917 --> 01:23:36.583
By the way,
I heard you can communicate with ghosts.

1248
01:23:37.042 --> 01:23:37.875
Yes, I can.

1249
01:23:37.958 --> 01:23:42.167
So, can you recognize a ghost
if it appears in front of you?

1250
01:23:43.042 --> 01:23:44.708
Yes, absolutely.

1251
01:23:44.792 --> 01:23:47.458
Interesting, very interesting.

1252
01:23:48.083 --> 01:23:51.083
Ms. Mandira,
we've prepared a special room for you.

1253
01:23:51.500 --> 01:23:53.667
- It used to belong to the king.
- Yes.

1254
01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:56.417
Can I stay in Manjulika's room instead?

1255
01:23:59.583 --> 01:24:00.583
Why?

1256
01:24:00.625 --> 01:24:01.625
Just because.

1257
01:24:02.083 --> 01:24:05.625
Staying in a room where
a ghost has been trapped for so long

1258
01:24:06.292 --> 01:24:09.042
would be quite the experience, right?

1259
01:24:10.292 --> 01:24:12.250
- Yes, that shouldn't be a problem.
- Okay.

1260
01:24:12.375 --> 01:24:13.936
- You should go straight and...
- I know.

1261
01:24:18.167 --> 01:24:19.292
She knows?

1262
01:24:19.458 --> 01:24:20.500
How does she know?

1263
01:25:35.208 --> 01:25:38.292
What's happening? What's going on?

1264
01:25:47.625 --> 01:25:48.625
What's going on?

1265
01:25:57.125 --> 01:25:58.125
He is here.

1266
01:25:59.125 --> 01:26:00.167
I knew this would happen.

1267
01:26:01.125 --> 01:26:02.875
This is the first sign of doom.

1268
01:26:05.042 --> 01:26:07.417
I warned you not to open that door.

1269
01:26:07.542 --> 01:26:09.208
Don't say that, Raj Purohit.

1270
01:26:10.000 --> 01:26:11.750
People are interested
in buying the palace.

1271
01:26:12.125 --> 01:26:14.167
If anyone gets wind of this,

1272
01:26:14.708 --> 01:26:16.375
it'll all fall apart.

1273
01:26:17.542 --> 01:26:19.583
Please, show us some mercy, Great Sage.

1274
01:26:20.208 --> 01:26:22.208
There's only one person
who can help you now.

1275
01:26:22.500 --> 01:26:23.500
Who?

1276
01:26:23.750 --> 01:26:24.750
And that person isn't me…

1277
01:26:25.792 --> 01:26:26.625
it's him.

1278
01:26:26.708 --> 01:26:27.917
This broomstick?

1279
01:26:28.000 --> 01:26:29.958
- Come again?
- Broomstick.

1280
01:26:30.167 --> 01:26:31.750
Why does it always have to be me?

1281
01:26:32.208 --> 01:26:33.333
How will I kill her?

1282
01:26:33.625 --> 01:26:37.542
You will kill her just like
Manjulika met her end in her past life.

1283
01:26:38.083 --> 01:26:38.917
You'll have to burn her.

1284
01:26:39.000 --> 01:26:40.083
But this time,

1285
01:26:40.625 --> 01:26:43.208
we are to turn not her body to ashes,
but her soul.

1286
01:26:44.083 --> 01:26:46.917
Using the wisdom
of our scriptures as my guide,

1287
01:26:47.125 --> 01:26:50.167
I'll perform the great ritual again,
just like my ancestors did.

1288
01:26:50.750 --> 01:26:54.250
The holy oil that comes
from the sacred fire

1289
01:26:55.083 --> 01:26:59.667
will be used to pen the final chapter
of Manjulika's story.

1290
01:26:59.750 --> 01:27:00.917
Great Sage!

1291
01:27:01.292 --> 01:27:02.292
But until then,

1292
01:27:03.125 --> 01:27:04.125
keep your guard up,

1293
01:27:05.000 --> 01:27:09.333
because I can sense
that she's been released.

1294
01:27:11.042 --> 01:27:12.167
Hey!

1295
01:27:14.333 --> 01:27:15.333
And she's watching…

1296
01:27:16.625 --> 01:27:17.750
all of you.

1297
01:27:32.333 --> 01:27:34.708
This is the most beautiful place
in our village.

1298
01:27:34.958 --> 01:27:37.833
All these temples that you see
are quite ancient.

1299
01:27:38.542 --> 01:27:39.375
Come, let's go inside!

1300
01:27:39.458 --> 01:27:40.458
I don't visit temples.

1301
01:27:41.667 --> 01:27:42.667
Why not?

1302
01:27:43.208 --> 01:27:44.625
I don't believe in God.

1303
01:27:45.125 --> 01:27:47.167
But your name means "temple," Ms. Mandira.

1304
01:27:47.625 --> 01:27:49.143
You could think of it as a tourist spot
and check it out.

1305
01:27:49.167 --> 01:27:50.792
I said I don't go to temples!

1306
01:27:58.750 --> 01:28:00.375
I'm sorry. I'm…

1307
01:28:01.000 --> 01:28:02.000
I'm an atheist.

1308
01:28:03.542 --> 01:28:04.542
Can we go somewhere else?

1309
01:28:06.417 --> 01:28:07.625
Sure. Let's go.

1310
01:28:14.667 --> 01:28:15.958
Greetings, everyone!

1311
01:28:17.000 --> 01:28:22.167
In our time of need, you all helped
us immensely and lent us money.

1312
01:28:22.292 --> 01:28:24.625
Now that our fortunes are looking up,

1313
01:28:25.167 --> 01:28:27.375
we can't forget you all.

1314
01:28:27.875 --> 01:28:29.375
So today,

1315
01:28:30.167 --> 01:28:31.250
on behalf of our family,

1316
01:28:31.333 --> 01:28:33.458
we're throwing a royal feast
for the whole village.

1317
01:28:34.750 --> 01:28:35.750
Enjoy!

1318
01:28:38.000 --> 01:28:39.000
Brother!

1319
01:28:40.292 --> 01:28:43.000
Money is tight,
and you're hosting a feast?

1320
01:28:43.583 --> 01:28:45.375
Where did you get all this chicken from?

1321
01:28:46.708 --> 01:28:49.250
It's not chicken, it's crow.

1322
01:28:49.333 --> 01:28:50.333
Crow?

1323
01:28:52.917 --> 01:28:55.542
A bunch of crows died
in the palace yesterday,

1324
01:28:56.083 --> 01:28:57.083
so we cooked them.

1325
01:28:57.417 --> 01:28:58.417
Crow biryani!

1326
01:29:07.750 --> 01:29:08.750
Hey, Ms. Mallika!

1327
01:29:09.292 --> 01:29:10.372
I see you are buying dolls!

1328
01:29:11.333 --> 01:29:12.917
Ms. Mallika, meet Ms. Mandira.

1329
01:29:19.583 --> 01:29:20.583
Nice to meet you.

1330
01:29:20.917 --> 01:29:21.917
Same here.

1331
01:29:22.333 --> 01:29:23.333
After you.

1332
01:29:26.458 --> 01:29:27.458
Nice to meet you.

1333
01:29:28.167 --> 01:29:29.583
Same here. After you.

1334
01:29:32.000 --> 01:29:35.792
<i>O' my beloved, my heart's delight</i>

1335
01:29:36.833 --> 01:29:40.417
<i>Look in my eyes and share
What in your heart lies</i>

1336
01:29:41.708 --> 01:29:46.167
<i>With every breath, I chant your name</i>

1337
01:29:46.375 --> 01:29:50.917
<i>For you, I live
And I'll die even if in vain</i>

1338
01:29:51.208 --> 01:29:55.750
<i>With every breath, I chant your name</i>

1339
01:29:56.000 --> 01:29:59.917
<i>For you, I live
And I'll die even if in vain</i>

1340
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:04.667
<i>My love
Please hear what my heart conveys</i>

1341
01:30:04.750 --> 01:30:09.458
<i>In your path, it forever stays</i>

1342
01:30:09.542 --> 01:30:14.208
<i>My love
Please hear what my heart conveys</i>

1343
01:30:14.292 --> 01:30:17.250
<i>In your arms, I wish to live my days</i>

1344
01:30:17.333 --> 01:30:19.792
<i>And in your love, I long to fade away</i>

1345
01:30:20.083 --> 01:30:23.750
<i>O' my beloved, my heart's delight</i>

1346
01:30:24.792 --> 01:30:28.583
<i>Look in my eyes
And share what in your heart lies</i>

1347
01:30:29.625 --> 01:30:34.125
<i>O' my beloved, my heart's delight</i>

1348
01:30:34.458 --> 01:30:38.208
<i>Hold me in your arms
And don't let me go, alright</i>

1349
01:30:48.750 --> 01:30:53.417
<i>These love's game
I have played them all from the start</i>

1350
01:30:53.625 --> 01:30:58.125
<i>I've spent lonely nights
Despite giving away my heart</i>

1351
01:30:58.375 --> 01:31:03.042
<i>I like you
For you are still a mystery to me</i>

1352
01:31:03.208 --> 01:31:07.083
<i>Otherwise, I've solved the toughest
Puzzles as they can be</i>

1353
01:31:07.167 --> 01:31:11.792
<i>My love
Please understand that I am afraid</i>

1354
01:31:11.875 --> 01:31:16.542
<i>I gaze at you from afar
And my heart's swayed</i>

1355
01:31:16.625 --> 01:31:21.417
<i>Please know that I am yours, my bae</i>

1356
01:31:21.500 --> 01:31:24.500
<i>In your dreams, I wish to live my days</i>

1357
01:31:24.583 --> 01:31:27.000
<i>And in your love, I long to fade away</i>

1358
01:31:27.208 --> 01:31:31.250
<i>Oh my</i>

1359
01:31:31.833 --> 01:31:35.750
<i>O' my beloved, my heart's delight</i>

1360
01:31:36.792 --> 01:31:40.708
<i>Look in my eyes
And share what in your heart lies</i>

1361
01:31:41.583 --> 01:31:46.167
<i>O' my beloved, my heart's delight</i>

1362
01:31:46.375 --> 01:31:50.375
<i>Hold me in your arms
And don't let me go, alright</i>

1363
01:32:43.250 --> 01:32:44.250
Party!

1364
01:32:44.417 --> 01:32:45.792
What's the occasion?

1365
01:32:45.875 --> 01:32:48.500
You've resolved all the palace issues.

1366
01:32:48.583 --> 01:32:49.583
Thank you.

1367
01:32:50.500 --> 01:32:51.500
Here's your cheque.

1368
01:32:52.292 --> 01:32:53.292
You may leave now.

1369
01:32:53.583 --> 01:32:54.458
- Leave?
- Leave?

1370
01:32:54.542 --> 01:32:56.917
The Howrah Express departs at ten.

1371
01:32:57.000 --> 01:32:59.000
You're running late.
Pack your bags and…

1372
01:33:16.042 --> 01:33:17.042
Savitri,

1373
01:33:17.625 --> 01:33:22.000
I'll commission a grand marble statue
in your honor.

1374
01:33:22.458 --> 01:33:24.125
Does he talk to souls too?

1375
01:33:25.125 --> 01:33:27.250
No, just my mother…

1376
01:33:27.792 --> 01:33:28.875
when he gets emotional.

1377
01:33:35.417 --> 01:33:36.542
I'm not with him.

1378
01:33:39.167 --> 01:33:40.167
Ruhaan!

1379
01:33:40.417 --> 01:33:41.417
What's all this nonsense?

1380
01:33:49.167 --> 01:33:50.847
Are you going to talk to me like this now?

1381
01:33:52.208 --> 01:33:55.167
Your heart has grown cold.

1382
01:33:56.333 --> 01:33:57.333
Hey…

1383
01:34:02.125 --> 01:34:04.292
Is your love dead too, like me?

1384
01:34:14.000 --> 01:34:16.667
Your Highness,
I forgot to mention something.

1385
01:34:17.708 --> 01:34:19.125
I don't just talk to souls,

1386
01:34:19.375 --> 01:34:21.042
they also take over me as a medium.

1387
01:34:21.958 --> 01:34:23.375
Don't interrupt.

1388
01:34:24.833 --> 01:34:25.833
Auntie, I'm just...

1389
01:34:26.417 --> 01:34:28.958
Keep quiet. I'm speaking to my husband.

1390
01:34:29.208 --> 01:34:30.375
Do not interfere.

1391
01:34:30.958 --> 01:34:32.625
Are you taking your pills every day?

1392
01:34:32.917 --> 01:34:33.917
Savitri?

1393
01:34:34.125 --> 01:34:35.125
Yes, I'm Savitri.

1394
01:34:35.167 --> 01:34:36.167
Auntie?

1395
01:34:39.333 --> 01:34:41.750
What were you saying, my love?

1396
01:34:42.208 --> 01:34:43.958
You want to build a marble statue of me

1397
01:34:44.042 --> 01:34:46.542
because you always treated me
like a servant?

1398
01:34:46.625 --> 01:34:47.875
- Savitri…
- Forget it!

1399
01:34:48.333 --> 01:34:49.833
I don't want a statue.

1400
01:34:50.250 --> 01:34:52.625
I just want a boy…

1401
01:34:52.958 --> 01:34:53.833
A boy?

1402
01:34:53.958 --> 01:34:55.583
- A boy?
- A boy?

1403
01:34:56.000 --> 01:34:57.167
For our daughter.

1404
01:34:58.875 --> 01:35:03.083
Every mother dreams
of her daughter getting married someday.

1405
01:35:03.667 --> 01:35:05.347
I've already found a boy for our daughter.

1406
01:35:05.958 --> 01:35:06.958
Who?

1407
01:35:07.250 --> 01:35:08.417
How about this one?

1408
01:35:10.500 --> 01:35:12.375
Mother? What are you doing?

1409
01:35:13.500 --> 01:35:14.792
You don't like her?

1410
01:35:15.292 --> 01:35:16.542
I like her, but…

1411
01:35:17.250 --> 01:35:19.250
Then let me speak to my husband.

1412
01:35:20.500 --> 01:35:23.333
I've seen this boy from within.

1413
01:35:23.583 --> 01:35:24.583
Really?

1414
01:35:24.708 --> 01:35:26.333
I possess him right now.

1415
01:35:26.833 --> 01:35:27.917
He's a gem.

1416
01:35:28.417 --> 01:35:29.292
Diamond.

1417
01:35:29.375 --> 01:35:30.375
Diamond.

1418
01:35:31.375 --> 01:35:34.583
Mother,
if you'd also ask what Meera wants...

1419
01:35:35.958 --> 01:35:36.958
You're right.

1420
01:35:37.333 --> 01:35:38.333
Meera…

1421
01:35:39.917 --> 01:35:40.917
Father…

1422
01:35:41.708 --> 01:35:42.708
Tell me the truth.

1423
01:35:43.458 --> 01:35:44.750
You love him, right?

1424
01:35:45.958 --> 01:35:46.958
Do you love him?

1425
01:35:48.583 --> 01:35:49.583
Yes, Mother.

1426
01:35:50.375 --> 01:35:51.375
I love him.

1427
01:35:52.083 --> 01:35:53.083
Done.

1428
01:35:53.417 --> 01:35:56.208
Let's quickly prepare for their wedding.

1429
01:35:56.417 --> 01:35:58.257
- My daughter is so beautiful.
- Wait a minute!

1430
01:36:00.708 --> 01:36:01.958
Uncle…

1431
01:36:07.208 --> 01:36:08.208
Sister!

1432
01:36:09.833 --> 01:36:10.833
Great choice?

1433
01:36:11.292 --> 01:36:12.458
Great choice, Sister.

1434
01:36:12.542 --> 01:36:13.708
Great choice!

1435
01:36:14.125 --> 01:36:15.125
Come here.

1436
01:36:21.958 --> 01:36:24.375
Hey, you guys still haven't
cleaned the room?

1437
01:36:25.208 --> 01:36:26.917
Hurry up, the buyers are coming.

1438
01:36:27.000 --> 01:36:29.542
Let them come.
Everything's clean.

1439
01:36:29.667 --> 01:36:30.542
Just a sec.

1440
01:36:30.625 --> 01:36:33.625
Hey, show her what you found
while tidying up this place.

1441
01:36:33.833 --> 01:36:35.292
These!

1442
01:36:35.375 --> 01:36:37.583
Hey, why are you showing
her the things we stole?

1443
01:36:37.667 --> 01:36:39.333
Did I show her that I took this?

1444
01:36:39.792 --> 01:36:41.000
Oh, I see!

1445
01:36:41.167 --> 01:36:43.917
Show her the important find…
I mean the painting.

1446
01:36:44.000 --> 01:36:46.333
According to my limited English,

1447
01:36:46.708 --> 01:36:50.125
it says "Princess Manjulika."

1448
01:36:53.000 --> 01:36:55.125
PRINCESS MANJULIKA

1449
01:36:56.917 --> 01:36:57.917
Unwrap it.

1450
01:37:04.583 --> 01:37:07.500
Now we can uncover Manjulika's secret.

1451
01:37:14.625 --> 01:37:15.625
Hey!

1452
01:37:16.917 --> 01:37:18.042
Oh no!

1453
01:37:18.333 --> 01:37:20.292
Sorry, sorry, sorry,
it slipped out of my hands.

1454
01:37:20.375 --> 01:37:21.542
Was it important?

1455
01:37:27.458 --> 01:37:29.018
Come on,
I just spilled a bit of paint on it.

1456
01:37:29.042 --> 01:37:32.083
You're looking at me as
if I've killed someone!

1457
01:37:35.625 --> 01:37:37.292
Where are you taking me, Uncle?

1458
01:37:37.375 --> 01:37:39.375
This room is full of royal clothes.

1459
01:37:39.458 --> 01:37:41.875
At your wedding,
you'll wear Debendra's Sherwani,

1460
01:37:41.958 --> 01:37:43.118
and I'll wear the Maharaja's.

1461
01:37:44.292 --> 01:37:45.417
Here you go!

1462
01:37:46.958 --> 01:37:47.958
- Bad!
- Bad!

1463
01:37:52.125 --> 01:37:54.000
It looks okay, but still not great.

1464
01:37:58.125 --> 01:37:59.583
Show us something cooler!

1465
01:38:00.083 --> 01:38:01.083
Something cooler?

1466
01:38:02.500 --> 01:38:04.458
Here.

1467
01:38:05.042 --> 01:38:06.482
- This is the one!
- This is the one!

1468
01:38:11.375 --> 01:38:12.625
Let me go!

1469
01:38:12.750 --> 01:38:14.667
Uncle has grabbed my neck!
Uncle, let me go!

1470
01:38:14.750 --> 01:38:16.375
Who will free me from her clutches?

1471
01:38:16.583 --> 01:38:18.417
Let me go! I'll die!

1472
01:38:23.708 --> 01:38:24.583
Ruhaan!

1473
01:38:24.667 --> 01:38:25.667
Ruhaan, I need your help!

1474
01:38:25.958 --> 01:38:27.542
Ruhaan, save me.

1475
01:38:27.958 --> 01:38:28.958
Let him go!

1476
01:38:29.167 --> 01:38:30.458
- Forget the Uncle!
- Shut up!

1477
01:38:30.542 --> 01:38:32.542
- Forget about him!
- Let me go!

1478
01:38:33.333 --> 01:38:34.792
Why are you hitting me?

1479
01:38:35.417 --> 01:38:36.500
Focus on the ghost!

1480
01:38:36.917 --> 01:38:38.333
She will kill me!

1481
01:38:38.708 --> 01:38:39.708
Uncle!

1482
01:38:39.917 --> 01:38:40.792
Come on!

1483
01:38:40.875 --> 01:38:41.750
Run!

1484
01:38:41.833 --> 01:38:43.167
Run! Run! Run!

1485
01:38:43.292 --> 01:38:45.667
- Ghost!
- How did this door close?

1486
01:38:47.875 --> 01:38:49.542
- Help us!
- Stop, sherwani!

1487
01:38:49.625 --> 01:38:51.042
We even called you cool.

1488
01:38:51.750 --> 01:38:53.250
Ruhaan, she's coming this way.

1489
01:38:53.333 --> 01:38:55.958
It's open. Ghost! Run!

1490
01:38:56.042 --> 01:38:57.042
Run!

1491
01:38:58.167 --> 01:38:59.167
Brother-in-law!

1492
01:38:59.208 --> 01:39:00.792
- Brother-in-law!
- What happened?

1493
01:39:01.583 --> 01:39:03.042
- Ghost!
- Ghost!

1494
01:39:03.333 --> 01:39:04.750
Ghost!

1495
01:39:17.875 --> 01:39:19.917
How could your boss, Mr. Rai think

1496
01:39:20.375 --> 01:39:22.583
I'd sell this palace
for such a low price?

1497
01:39:22.667 --> 01:39:23.583
Brother-in-law!

1498
01:39:23.667 --> 01:39:24.500
Ghost!

1499
01:39:24.583 --> 01:39:25.583
- Ghost!
- Ghost!

1500
01:39:25.667 --> 01:39:26.500
Ghost!

1501
01:39:26.583 --> 01:39:28.500
- Ghost!
- Yes, I've been saying the same thing!

1502
01:39:28.583 --> 01:39:30.208
There's no ghost here anymore!

1503
01:39:30.292 --> 01:39:31.583
This is a prime property,

1504
01:39:31.667 --> 01:39:34.750
and he's offering only
eight billion rupees.

1505
01:39:34.917 --> 01:39:36.333
- Eight billion?
- Eight billion?

1506
01:39:36.625 --> 01:39:37.625
Did you see it?

1507
01:39:38.000 --> 01:39:39.500
Look at him sweating!

1508
01:39:39.583 --> 01:39:40.833
You've quoted such a low price!

1509
01:39:40.917 --> 01:39:41.750
Take your cheque back!

1510
01:39:41.833 --> 01:39:43.351
You're making a mistake, Your Highness.

1511
01:39:43.375 --> 01:39:44.375
You're right.

1512
01:39:47.583 --> 01:39:48.583
This…

1513
01:39:48.667 --> 01:39:49.667
Okay?

1514
01:39:49.958 --> 01:39:51.083
Now, get out!

1515
01:39:51.458 --> 01:39:52.292
Leave!

1516
01:39:52.375 --> 01:39:53.500
What have you done?

1517
01:39:53.667 --> 01:39:55.375
- Excuse me, sir…
- Brother-in-law,

1518
01:39:55.458 --> 01:39:57.875
Manjulika's ghost hasn't left
this palace.

1519
01:39:57.958 --> 01:40:00.042
She just tried to kill me!
Look over here.

1520
01:40:00.125 --> 01:40:01.206
What are you talking about?

1521
01:40:01.458 --> 01:40:02.518
He got rid of her, didn't he?

1522
01:40:02.542 --> 01:40:05.208
How can he make her leave
if he's scared of ghosts too?

1523
01:40:05.292 --> 01:40:06.792
Exactly, he's no Baba.

1524
01:40:06.875 --> 01:40:08.083
You're right, Your Highness.

1525
01:40:09.042 --> 01:40:11.083
Actually, I'm not anyone's reincarnation.

1526
01:40:11.167 --> 01:40:13.917
Forget ghosts, spirits, or witches…

1527
01:40:14.500 --> 01:40:16.833
I'm even scared of rats!

1528
01:40:17.333 --> 01:40:18.500
You won't understand.

1529
01:40:19.042 --> 01:40:19.958
Your Highness?

1530
01:40:20.042 --> 01:40:21.042
Where is he?

1531
01:40:21.625 --> 01:40:22.958
Someone get me some tape!

1532
01:40:23.875 --> 01:40:26.083
It's in pieces now, Your Highness.

1533
01:40:27.583 --> 01:40:29.875
I'll tear you to pieces!

1534
01:40:30.542 --> 01:40:31.667
- Father!
- Brother-in-law!

1535
01:40:31.750 --> 01:40:33.042
You fake Crown Prince!

1536
01:40:33.125 --> 01:40:37.083
- Your Highness!
- You pretended to be Savitri!

1537
01:40:37.458 --> 01:40:39.125
You can hit me later, Your Highness.

1538
01:40:39.792 --> 01:40:42.392
First, we need to figure out how
to save ourselves from Manjulika.

1539
01:40:44.708 --> 01:40:48.167
Brother, let's just leave this palace!

1540
01:40:48.250 --> 01:40:49.833
- No way!
- Why not?

1541
01:40:49.917 --> 01:40:51.125
- Poverty.
- Come on!

1542
01:40:51.708 --> 01:40:54.625
I can't live on scraps anymore.

1543
01:40:55.458 --> 01:40:57.250
Even if Manjulika eats me,

1544
01:40:57.917 --> 01:40:59.667
I won't leave until this palace is sold.

1545
01:41:00.292 --> 01:41:02.083
- No.
- Then let's sell it and run.

1546
01:41:02.625 --> 01:41:03.708
To whom?

1547
01:41:04.125 --> 01:41:05.125
You know…

1548
01:41:05.833 --> 01:41:07.125
Her Highness Mandira!

1549
01:41:07.875 --> 01:41:09.833
She has no idea about the ghost.

1550
01:41:10.583 --> 01:41:13.292
I tricked you, you can trick her.

1551
01:41:13.583 --> 01:41:14.917
Let's sell the palace to her!

1552
01:41:16.583 --> 01:41:17.708
You…

1553
01:41:18.375 --> 01:41:19.375
No!

1554
01:41:21.542 --> 01:41:24.458
Ms. Mandira,
we've given you a tour of the palace,

1555
01:41:24.542 --> 01:41:26.833
shown you around the village,
and taken you to the fair.

1556
01:41:26.917 --> 01:41:28.643
So, how much longer
are we going to drag this out?

1557
01:41:28.667 --> 01:41:30.143
Just buy the palace and be done with it.

1558
01:41:30.167 --> 01:41:31.833
I really liked the palace, actually.

1559
01:41:32.125 --> 01:41:35.000
That's why I got all the paperwork
ready with my lawyer.

1560
01:41:35.083 --> 01:41:36.375
Oh, that's great!

1561
01:41:36.458 --> 01:41:38.708
But I'm not paying
a penny over ten billion!

1562
01:41:40.125 --> 01:41:41.542
It's all good, Brother-in-law.

1563
01:41:41.625 --> 01:41:43.268
I know it's a bit less than you
were hoping for, but we'll manage.

1564
01:41:43.292 --> 01:41:44.643
- It's fine.
- We really don't have time to waste.

1565
01:41:44.667 --> 01:41:45.726
- It's okay.
- Yes, Dad. It's okay.

1566
01:41:45.750 --> 01:41:47.071
- You can have this palace.
- Yes!

1567
01:41:47.125 --> 01:41:48.434
- Let's go and pack.
- Let's go, let's go, let's go.

1568
01:41:48.458 --> 01:41:50.167
I just have one small condition.

1569
01:41:50.875 --> 01:41:53.667
- What's that now?
- I want to buy the palace in two days,

1570
01:41:53.875 --> 01:41:55.583
- on Durga Ashtami.
- Hey…

1571
01:41:55.667 --> 01:41:56.851
- Wait, two days?
- On Durga Ashtami?

1572
01:41:56.875 --> 01:41:57.875
That'll be too late!

1573
01:41:57.917 --> 01:41:59.708
No, you should buy it right away.

1574
01:41:59.792 --> 01:42:00.917
It's a very auspicious day.

1575
01:42:01.792 --> 01:42:03.708
Sorry, but I can't do
a deal before that.

1576
01:42:04.250 --> 01:42:05.083
Oh no.

1577
01:42:05.167 --> 01:42:07.417
Then you can finalize the deal with me.

1578
01:42:10.458 --> 01:42:12.458
Brother-in-law, this is Vicky Khanna,

1579
01:42:13.417 --> 01:42:15.250
the owner of the Zodiac group of hotels.

1580
01:42:15.458 --> 01:42:16.458
He's really wealthy.

1581
01:42:16.500 --> 01:42:17.833
He appears on Shark Tank.

1582
01:42:17.917 --> 01:42:19.167
- Shark Tank?
- Oh!

1583
01:42:19.792 --> 01:42:21.708
Why don't you make us an offer then?

1584
01:42:21.833 --> 01:42:25.083
Your Highness,
I love this property of yours.

1585
01:42:25.167 --> 01:42:27.833
And I am willing
to pay you the right price for it.

1586
01:42:27.917 --> 01:42:29.083
The right price!

1587
01:42:29.500 --> 01:42:31.083
- Good.
- She offered us ten billion.

1588
01:42:31.292 --> 01:42:32.292
I'll match that.

1589
01:42:32.958 --> 01:42:33.958
You will?

1590
01:42:34.292 --> 01:42:35.792
She'll finalize the deal in two days.

1591
01:42:35.875 --> 01:42:37.309
- I can finalize it right now!
- What are you saying?!

1592
01:42:37.333 --> 01:42:39.958
- Right now.
- Please come with us. Let's go.

1593
01:42:40.042 --> 01:42:41.458
Come. Bring snacks.

1594
01:42:41.542 --> 01:42:42.542
Shark Tank's…

1595
01:42:58.875 --> 01:43:01.583
Wow, what a good-looking chair!

1596
01:43:02.250 --> 01:43:03.333
What a great design!

1597
01:43:03.708 --> 01:43:04.792
I love it!

1598
01:43:04.875 --> 01:43:05.875
It's actually a throne.

1599
01:43:07.167 --> 01:43:09.792
It used to belong to the king.

1600
01:43:10.500 --> 01:43:12.875
Can you please have the staff load
it into my car?

1601
01:43:12.958 --> 01:43:16.208
I think it will look beautiful in my…

1602
01:43:16.833 --> 01:43:17.833
drawing room.

1603
01:43:18.625 --> 01:43:20.545
This throne is a big part
of this palace's pride.

1604
01:43:21.458 --> 01:43:22.833
It's part of the heritage.

1605
01:43:23.292 --> 01:43:25.458
Excuse me, ma'am,
but I'm buying this palace,

1606
01:43:25.708 --> 01:43:28.509
so everything here belongs to me,
and I can do whatever I want with it.

1607
01:43:28.833 --> 01:43:30.083
Who is she anyway?

1608
01:43:30.708 --> 01:43:31.750
That's Ms. Mallika.

1609
01:43:32.042 --> 01:43:33.667
She's been restoring the palace.

1610
01:43:33.958 --> 01:43:34.958
Oh!

1611
01:43:35.333 --> 01:43:40.292
Well, you're not needed anymore
because I don't want to restore it.

1612
01:43:40.375 --> 01:43:43.542
I want to redesign it.

1613
01:43:44.625 --> 01:43:47.417
And this place won't be
a king's court anymore…

1614
01:43:48.292 --> 01:43:50.125
it'll be a bar!

1615
01:44:01.708 --> 01:44:02.708
Bye.

1616
01:44:03.542 --> 01:44:05.917
Hey, be careful! Easy there!
Bring it with care.

1617
01:44:06.000 --> 01:44:07.042
Alright, Your Highness.

1618
01:44:07.583 --> 01:44:09.208
I'll take your leave.

1619
01:44:11.917 --> 01:44:14.037
This palace will officially
be mine starting tomorrow.

1620
01:44:14.083 --> 01:44:15.083
Of course!

1621
01:44:21.583 --> 01:44:25.583
<i>How did you come to be in my days?</i>

1622
01:44:27.500 --> 01:44:31.208
<i>I can't believe fate!</i>

1623
01:46:04.833 --> 01:46:05.833
Mallika?

1624
01:46:07.417 --> 01:46:10.458
Mallika, how did this throne
end up back here?

1625
01:46:12.667 --> 01:46:15.167
Mallika, I asked you a question.

1626
01:46:17.792 --> 01:46:18.917
Why are you sitting on it?

1627
01:46:19.000 --> 01:46:20.500
Shut up, you obnoxious women!

1628
01:46:22.917 --> 01:46:24.208
Witch!

1629
01:46:25.000 --> 01:46:26.208
Brainless twit!

1630
01:46:27.500 --> 01:46:29.792
How dare you give my throne to him?!

1631
01:46:30.250 --> 01:46:32.292
How dare you!

1632
01:46:32.958 --> 01:46:35.042
How many times will you snatch
it away from me?

1633
01:46:36.125 --> 01:46:38.083
This throne belongs to me!

1634
01:46:38.500 --> 01:46:42.875
This throne is mine!
It's mine!

1635
01:46:43.833 --> 01:46:46.417
Anyone who tries to touch it,

1636
01:46:46.750 --> 01:46:50.292
I'll slit their throat
and drink their blood!

1637
01:46:51.625 --> 01:46:54.000
This is my throne!

1638
01:46:54.792 --> 01:46:56.458
Father!

1639
01:46:58.583 --> 01:47:00.500
Ruhaan, she…

1640
01:47:00.583 --> 01:47:02.000
Mallika, in there…

1641
01:47:02.542 --> 01:47:03.583
Yes, Meera, what is it?

1642
01:47:05.458 --> 01:47:06.458
You are here?

1643
01:47:06.500 --> 01:47:07.917
But you were just in there.

1644
01:47:08.375 --> 01:47:09.375
Where?

1645
01:47:09.625 --> 01:47:10.705
I've been here for a while.

1646
01:47:11.292 --> 01:47:12.292
Ruhaan…

1647
01:47:12.708 --> 01:47:13.708
Listen, Meera.

1648
01:47:13.958 --> 01:47:15.750
Do you know he's dead?

1649
01:47:16.583 --> 01:47:17.417
Who?

1650
01:47:17.500 --> 01:47:19.708
Vicky Khanna is dead.

1651
01:47:30.667 --> 01:47:31.667
He's dead!

1652
01:47:33.333 --> 01:47:35.250
Oh, I'm sorry.

1653
01:47:36.250 --> 01:47:37.250
It's very rude.

1654
01:47:38.917 --> 01:47:41.583
Here's the contract.

1655
01:47:44.583 --> 01:47:48.792
I had a feeling that the deal
wouldn't go through.

1656
01:47:50.833 --> 01:47:53.583
So, should we sign it in two days?

1657
01:47:54.000 --> 01:47:55.125
On Durga Ashtami?

1658
01:47:57.833 --> 01:47:58.833
He's dead!

1659
01:48:00.750 --> 01:48:01.750
He's dead!

1660
01:48:08.083 --> 01:48:10.208
Who laughs like that
when they hear someone has died?

1661
01:48:12.292 --> 01:48:13.792
I think she's really strange.

1662
01:48:17.542 --> 01:48:19.667
Honestly, I find both of them odd.

1663
01:48:20.542 --> 01:48:21.917
They should see a doctor.

1664
01:48:23.083 --> 01:48:25.917
Ever since she showed up,
things have been a bit weird around here.

1665
01:48:27.083 --> 01:48:28.483
I was just thinking the same thing!

1666
01:48:30.417 --> 01:48:31.417
I've got a feeling that…

1667
01:48:31.500 --> 01:48:32.500
She might be Manjulika.

1668
01:48:34.000 --> 01:48:35.000
Yes.

1669
01:48:35.708 --> 01:48:38.589
Remember how she got all anxious
when we asked her to go into the temple?

1670
01:48:39.125 --> 01:48:40.458
She doesn't believe in God,

1671
01:48:40.833 --> 01:48:42.994
but she wants to seal the palace deal
on Durga Ashtami.

1672
01:48:43.667 --> 01:48:44.750
Who are you talking about?

1673
01:48:45.375 --> 01:48:46.375
Mandira.

1674
01:48:46.667 --> 01:48:48.792
I'm talking about Mallika.

1675
01:48:48.875 --> 01:48:50.958
Why are you suspicious
of that poor woman?

1676
01:48:51.292 --> 01:48:52.792
She calls me her little brother.

1677
01:48:52.875 --> 01:48:55.083
Exactly! Isn't that a clear enough hint?

1678
01:48:55.750 --> 01:48:57.667
You didn't see how she looked
at Vicky Khanna

1679
01:48:57.750 --> 01:49:00.708
with such anger when he talked
about taking the throne.

1680
01:49:00.792 --> 01:49:03.125
Oh, Mandira shot him
a look of pure hatred

1681
01:49:03.583 --> 01:49:05.708
when he took the palace deal from her.

1682
01:49:05.792 --> 01:49:08.542
You don't believe me when
I say she lifted the throne, right?

1683
01:49:08.625 --> 01:49:09.986
How am I supposed to believe that?

1684
01:49:10.125 --> 01:49:11.708
Mallika was with me when it happened.

1685
01:49:11.833 --> 01:49:14.354
Fine, don't believe me,
but I really think Mallika is Manjulika.

1686
01:49:15.458 --> 01:49:16.458
I'm telling you,

1687
01:49:17.917 --> 01:49:19.167
Mandira is Manjulika.

1688
01:50:56.542 --> 01:50:58.417
"We stole mangoes on the sly."

1689
01:50:58.500 --> 01:51:00.458
The spicy masala in <i>pani puri</i> was oh my!

1690
01:51:00.542 --> 01:51:02.309
The <i>pani puri</i> was so good
we couldn't let it pass by.

1691
01:51:02.333 --> 01:51:04.042
We then gave fish a try.

1692
01:51:04.125 --> 01:51:06.000
Out from the fish, a thorn did fly.

1693
01:51:06.083 --> 01:51:08.083
Grandma gave us a slap, I wonder why!

1694
01:51:11.208 --> 01:51:12.833
Out came the blood from the slap wound.

1695
01:51:13.375 --> 01:51:15.208
Quickly use the telephone.

1696
01:51:15.292 --> 01:51:17.292
But no wire can be
found at the telephone's end.

1697
01:51:17.458 --> 01:51:20.208
"Trust me, I'm not your friend!"

1698
01:51:28.208 --> 01:51:29.208
What's wrong?

1699
01:51:31.333 --> 01:51:32.750
You are wondering

1700
01:51:34.042 --> 01:51:38.125
which one of us is Manjulika, aren't you?

1701
01:51:39.542 --> 01:51:41.208
I'm Manjulika!

1702
01:51:41.875 --> 01:51:43.333
I'm Manjulika!

1703
01:51:44.042 --> 01:51:45.417
I'm Manjulika!

1704
01:51:45.500 --> 01:51:46.792
I'm Manjulika!

1705
01:51:46.875 --> 01:51:48.167
I'm Manjulika!

1706
01:51:54.417 --> 01:51:55.417
That was close!

1707
01:52:44.250 --> 01:52:45.250
Look…

1708
01:53:20.708 --> 01:53:21.708
What's happening?

1709
01:53:24.792 --> 01:53:27.184
Forgive me, God. I promise
to stop doing wrong things from now on.

1710
01:53:27.208 --> 01:53:28.917
I started dating a witch for money.

1711
01:53:29.917 --> 01:53:33.083
"Ghosts and demons stay away."

1712
01:53:33.167 --> 01:53:34.583
Ghosts and demons stay away.

1713
01:53:35.000 --> 01:53:36.750
"Ghosts and demons stay away."

1714
01:53:36.833 --> 01:53:38.074
What have I gotten myself into?

1715
01:53:38.708 --> 01:53:41.500
"Ghosts and demons stay away."

1716
01:53:43.792 --> 01:53:44.708
- Pundit…
- Yes?

1717
01:53:44.792 --> 01:53:47.500
The atmosphere in this palace
is feeling pretty dangerous.

1718
01:53:47.833 --> 01:53:48.667
What happened?

1719
01:53:48.750 --> 01:53:50.917
I saw a witch on the terrace yesterday.

1720
01:53:51.125 --> 01:53:52.625
What are you saying?

1721
01:53:52.708 --> 01:53:54.125
She was hanging out laundry.

1722
01:53:54.208 --> 01:53:55.208
That was me!

1723
01:53:55.292 --> 01:53:58.792
How many times have I told you not
to walk around with your hair down?

1724
01:53:59.583 --> 01:54:01.601
There's no such thing as ghosts,
spirits, or witches!

1725
01:54:01.625 --> 01:54:02.625
You're right.

1726
01:54:02.833 --> 01:54:05.226
If there really was a Manjulika,
we would've found her by now.

1727
01:54:05.250 --> 01:54:08.708
My dream of hugging her
is still just a dream.

1728
01:54:08.792 --> 01:54:10.625
So then, how did Vicky Khanna die?

1729
01:54:10.792 --> 01:54:11.792
Nonsense!

1730
01:54:12.083 --> 01:54:13.500
Vicky Khanna isn't dead.

1731
01:54:15.833 --> 01:54:18.083
He's sitting right over there in a suit.

1732
01:54:21.917 --> 01:54:23.167
Hello, sir!

1733
01:54:24.083 --> 01:54:25.583
We were just talking about you.

1734
01:54:25.667 --> 01:54:27.458
You're going to have a long life.

1735
01:54:27.667 --> 01:54:28.875
Take good care of him.

1736
01:54:29.542 --> 01:54:34.792
You should've taken the three
of us instead of that throne.

1737
01:54:34.958 --> 01:54:38.750
We'd give you a service you wouldn't
even get in heaven after you die.

1738
01:54:38.833 --> 01:54:40.583
And we're not greedy or anything either.

1739
01:54:40.667 --> 01:54:43.125
Just give us three million
whenever you're happy with us.

1740
01:54:43.333 --> 01:54:44.750
Of course, he will.

1741
01:54:44.833 --> 01:54:46.958
If you please him, he will.

1742
01:54:47.250 --> 01:54:48.875
Right, sir.

1743
01:54:49.500 --> 01:54:51.101
You know that Junior Pundit
is a real piece of work.

1744
01:54:51.125 --> 01:54:55.417
His arms are longer than the law's reach.

1745
01:54:55.833 --> 01:54:57.875
Don't you think his arms are way too long?

1746
01:55:01.000 --> 01:55:03.500
I can sense a lot of tension in your neck.

1747
01:55:03.667 --> 01:55:05.458
Want me to give it a twist?

1748
01:55:18.833 --> 01:55:19.833
What's going on?

1749
01:55:20.417 --> 01:55:21.817
He just turned around and sat down.

1750
01:55:36.375 --> 01:55:38.792
Mr. Vicky, you were a great guy.

1751
01:55:39.042 --> 01:55:40.167
You <i>are</i>!

1752
01:55:40.500 --> 01:55:43.208
But we're loyal to His Highness.

1753
01:55:43.458 --> 01:55:45.917
Even though we barely
eat once every two days,

1754
01:55:46.333 --> 01:55:48.518
loyalty still counts, right?
I'm the one who cooks for us.

1755
01:55:48.542 --> 01:55:50.875
We can't betray him, sir.

1756
01:55:51.458 --> 01:55:52.458
You should really go.

1757
01:55:52.583 --> 01:55:53.667
Nice to meet you.

1758
01:55:54.875 --> 01:55:56.417
Hey!

1759
01:55:56.500 --> 01:55:59.583
- Mr. Ghost…
- Let go!

1760
01:56:00.875 --> 01:56:02.792
- Let go!
- Oh, my God!

1761
01:56:03.083 --> 01:56:04.083
Run…

1762
01:56:14.750 --> 01:56:17.750
She's calling you for a hug.

1763
01:56:19.875 --> 01:56:21.708
No, sister, no!
No, sister!

1764
01:56:21.792 --> 01:56:23.792
- No, sister!
- Oh God!

1765
01:56:29.083 --> 01:56:30.083
Hey,

1766
01:56:30.708 --> 01:56:32.292
who turned on Netflix?

1767
01:56:37.708 --> 01:56:38.708
Hello.

1768
01:56:39.500 --> 01:56:43.542
<i>I'll take your sweets, oh sweet one</i>

1769
01:56:44.125 --> 01:56:46.750
<i>You foreigner</i>

1770
01:56:46.833 --> 01:56:48.083
She's singing a Bengali song.

1771
01:56:48.167 --> 01:56:51.208
<i>You're just a foreigner up to this point</i>

1772
01:56:53.208 --> 01:56:54.208
Hey,

1773
01:56:54.792 --> 01:56:57.125
did you sleep in my room last night?

1774
01:56:58.083 --> 01:56:59.083
No.

1775
01:57:02.125 --> 01:57:05.167
No, you woke up, laughed,

1776
01:57:05.833 --> 01:57:06.953
and then went back to sleep.

1777
01:57:07.750 --> 01:57:08.750
I laughed?

1778
01:57:12.583 --> 01:57:13.583
Like this?

1779
01:57:15.833 --> 01:57:16.833
I'll be right back.

1780
01:57:17.542 --> 01:57:19.250
I told you it's not her.

1781
01:57:19.833 --> 01:57:20.954
He just wouldn't believe me.

1782
01:57:21.333 --> 01:57:22.750
He was doubting her for no reason.

1783
01:57:27.708 --> 01:57:29.708
- Ghostbuster!
- Hey! Get us out!

1784
01:57:33.667 --> 01:57:36.625
- Can't he hear us?
- Open it!

1785
01:57:38.833 --> 01:57:39.917
Death is at the door,

1786
01:57:40.167 --> 01:57:41.625
and they can't stop dancing!

1787
01:57:42.000 --> 01:57:43.976
Dance your hearts out,
you rascals. I'm out of here.

1788
01:57:44.000 --> 01:57:45.458
I'm done for!

1789
01:57:46.958 --> 01:57:48.500
Ruhaan?! Where are you going?

1790
01:57:49.833 --> 01:57:51.667
What happened?
Why aren't you saying anything?

1791
01:57:52.542 --> 01:57:55.083
We're getting married, Ruhaan.

1792
01:57:56.333 --> 01:57:57.417
Come on, head upstairs.

1793
01:57:59.042 --> 01:58:00.042
Get lost!

1794
01:58:03.167 --> 01:58:04.167
Father!

1795
01:58:04.917 --> 01:58:07.000
Father, Ruhaan has left us all.

1796
01:58:07.583 --> 01:58:08.583
That's great!

1797
01:58:09.208 --> 01:58:10.208
That's great!

1798
01:58:10.625 --> 01:58:13.542
At least Manjulika did one thing right.
She killed him.

1799
01:58:13.625 --> 01:58:16.208
He's not dead.
He's just left the palace.

1800
01:58:17.292 --> 01:58:18.625
That's good for you.

1801
01:58:18.917 --> 01:58:20.750
I never liked that guy.

1802
01:58:20.833 --> 01:58:22.500
Get out of my way!
He's going to die!

1803
01:58:22.667 --> 01:58:23.667
He's going to die!

1804
01:58:24.083 --> 01:58:25.125
What are you staring at?

1805
01:58:25.500 --> 01:58:28.100
You'll be held guilty if he dies.
Grab him and put him in the car.

1806
01:58:31.583 --> 01:58:32.625
What happened, Brother?

1807
01:58:33.250 --> 01:58:34.667
Nothing. I just needed to say that.

1808
01:59:00.042 --> 01:59:01.042
Your shoe!

1809
01:59:05.875 --> 01:59:07.292
What's going on?

1810
01:59:19.958 --> 01:59:21.833
Who are you waiting for?

1811
01:59:21.917 --> 01:59:23.125
Why aren't you leaving?

1812
01:59:23.500 --> 01:59:25.375
I can't find my way out of this maze.

1813
01:59:25.708 --> 01:59:27.958
I can't leave! I just can't!

1814
01:59:35.042 --> 01:59:36.375
- We are safe.
- We can run.

1815
01:59:36.667 --> 01:59:38.250
Run, Junior Pundit!

1816
01:59:38.333 --> 01:59:41.125
Your horoscope predicts death
for you today.

1817
01:59:44.625 --> 01:59:45.625
You?!

1818
01:59:48.167 --> 01:59:49.292
You left, right?

1819
01:59:49.917 --> 01:59:50.917
I couldn't leave.

1820
01:59:51.583 --> 01:59:52.583
I just couldn't leave…

1821
01:59:53.292 --> 01:59:54.292
you behind.

1822
01:59:55.458 --> 01:59:57.083
And all of you.

1823
01:59:57.417 --> 01:59:58.958
You are my family now.

1824
01:59:59.042 --> 02:00:00.042
You are my dear ones,

1825
02:00:00.250 --> 02:00:02.583
and dear ones always stick together.

1826
02:00:02.667 --> 02:00:05.167
Our daughter found such a gem
of a person.

1827
02:00:05.333 --> 02:00:06.333
Kohinoor!

1828
02:00:09.458 --> 02:00:10.458
Let's eat!

1829
02:00:10.542 --> 02:00:11.662
- Yeah, let's go!
- Let's go!

1830
02:00:11.792 --> 02:00:13.875
Let's eat before we become
someone else's meal.

1831
02:00:14.125 --> 02:00:15.125
Buzz off!

1832
02:00:16.458 --> 02:00:18.083
- Meera…
- Don't talk to me!

1833
02:00:18.375 --> 02:00:19.893
- Okay, so who should I talk to?
- Talk to us.

1834
02:00:19.917 --> 02:00:21.559
Seriously?
Why did you come back, you fool?

1835
02:00:21.583 --> 02:00:23.250
We are all doomed here.

1836
02:00:23.625 --> 02:00:25.042
Anyone could turn into Manjulika.

1837
02:00:25.125 --> 02:00:26.125
We are leaving.

1838
02:00:26.333 --> 02:00:27.333
Will you be able to?

1839
02:00:27.500 --> 02:00:29.434
Why wouldn't we be able to leave?
God gave us legs!

1840
02:00:29.458 --> 02:00:32.000
And our Rolls Royce is right here too.
He's just making excuses!

1841
02:00:32.083 --> 02:00:33.917
Alright, see you in a bit.

1842
02:00:35.250 --> 02:00:36.917
- What was that?
- Let's go, guys.

1843
02:00:37.333 --> 02:00:38.333
Hold this.

1844
02:00:38.583 --> 02:00:40.208
- Here, take it.
- What's this? Why?

1845
02:00:40.292 --> 02:00:42.625
Because we caught Manjulika's attention!

1846
02:00:42.708 --> 02:00:44.309
- Right!
- If we wear this, she won't recognize us.

1847
02:00:44.333 --> 02:00:45.167
Cover your face.

1848
02:00:45.250 --> 02:00:47.059
- Yes, yes, yes. That's perfect!
- I can't see anything.

1849
02:00:47.083 --> 02:00:48.083
Reverse the car.

1850
02:00:48.708 --> 02:00:50.829
You've checked the air pressure
and everything, right?

1851
02:01:00.458 --> 02:01:01.625
- What's going on?
- Oh no!

1852
02:01:01.708 --> 02:01:03.250
We're back to the same place!

1853
02:01:03.375 --> 02:01:06.042
Why'd you bring us back here, you fool?

1854
02:01:06.167 --> 02:01:07.167
I didn't!

1855
02:01:07.208 --> 02:01:08.917
- Let's get out of here!
- Let's go!

1856
02:01:09.250 --> 02:01:10.667
Hey! Rolls! Royce!

1857
02:01:18.417 --> 02:01:22.167
The engine got separated from the car.

1858
02:01:22.375 --> 02:01:23.667
My buffaloes!

1859
02:01:23.833 --> 02:01:25.708
You blockhead, what have you done?

1860
02:01:25.792 --> 02:01:26.792
Take off the goggles!

1861
02:01:27.667 --> 02:01:29.708
- We'll die!
- Where are Rolls and Royce?

1862
02:01:43.250 --> 02:01:45.417
Chotiya!

1863
02:01:45.500 --> 02:01:48.375
I told you your horoscope
stated you'd die today!

1864
02:01:48.625 --> 02:01:50.500
And he bloody died a virgin.

1865
02:01:50.583 --> 02:01:54.583
Save me, Mother Durga!

1866
02:02:00.167 --> 02:02:01.417
This is the sacred oil…

1867
02:02:02.750 --> 02:02:04.583
you'll use to eliminate Manjulika.

1868
02:02:05.042 --> 02:02:08.542
But he's not the reincarnated prince.

1869
02:02:09.292 --> 02:02:10.958
Do you know what he did in the city?

1870
02:02:11.083 --> 02:02:14.167
He pretended to talk
to ghosts and trick people.

1871
02:02:14.792 --> 02:02:15.792
You knew?

1872
02:02:16.208 --> 02:02:18.250
I knew the truth from the very first day.

1873
02:02:18.583 --> 02:02:22.958
And I also know my ancestor's
prophecies are never wrong.

1874
02:02:23.292 --> 02:02:26.042
Alright, let's say for a moment that
I am the reincarnated prince.

1875
02:02:26.333 --> 02:02:27.654
But who should I use this oil on,

1876
02:02:27.958 --> 02:02:29.125
Mandira or Mallika?

1877
02:02:29.250 --> 02:02:33.792
- What?
- So you think one of them is Manjulika?

1878
02:02:34.042 --> 02:02:37.500
Strange things have been happening
since they came here.

1879
02:02:37.792 --> 02:02:40.375
Faulad Singh, you've lived a long life.

1880
02:02:40.458 --> 02:02:42.375
Manjulika has played on your lap.

1881
02:02:42.458 --> 02:02:45.125
Tell us who the real Manjulika is.
We need to know quickly.

1882
02:02:45.208 --> 02:02:47.833
I don't know.
I can't remember anything, Pundit.

1883
02:02:48.000 --> 02:02:49.000
I'll tell you.

1884
02:02:49.083 --> 02:02:51.083
I found Manjulika's painting,

1885
02:02:51.250 --> 02:02:54.417
the one on which your
Mallika accidentally spilled the paint.

1886
02:02:54.750 --> 02:02:56.792
I sent it to the city to get cleaned.

1887
02:02:56.958 --> 02:02:58.917
Stupid girl,
you should have given it to me.

1888
02:02:59.000 --> 02:03:00.625
I would have cleaned it with soap.

1889
02:03:00.708 --> 02:03:02.708
Paintings can't be washed with soap,
you fool.

1890
02:03:02.792 --> 02:03:04.917
They're cleaned using special
chemicals in a lab.

1891
02:03:06.667 --> 02:03:08.042
We just need to wait a day.

1892
02:03:09.167 --> 02:03:10.567
We'll find out everything tomorrow.

1893
02:03:10.750 --> 02:03:11.750
Tomorrow?

1894
02:03:13.917 --> 02:03:14.958
You mean on Durga Ashtami?

1895
02:03:23.750 --> 02:03:26.833
We can only get rid of the fake ghosts
by dressing up as a <i>baba</i>.

1896
02:03:26.917 --> 02:03:28.250
Manjulika is a witch!

1897
02:03:28.708 --> 02:03:29.750
You won't understand.

1898
02:03:31.125 --> 02:03:32.205
It gives me the right feel.

1899
02:03:33.167 --> 02:03:34.875
Only that sacred oil can save us now.

1900
02:03:34.958 --> 02:03:37.417
Just go and check if that cleaned
painting has come back.

1901
02:03:42.458 --> 02:03:43.458
Where did that oil go?

1902
02:03:51.833 --> 02:03:52.917
What are you two doing?

1903
02:03:53.125 --> 02:03:55.417
Hey, Ghostbuster!

1904
02:03:56.000 --> 02:03:59.625
My hair has been infested
with lice since childhood.

1905
02:03:59.750 --> 02:04:01.268
My mother even died trying
to get rid of them,

1906
02:04:01.292 --> 02:04:02.393
but the lice just won't go away.

1907
02:04:02.417 --> 02:04:03.934
What was that oil we used to use,
sweetheart?

1908
02:04:03.958 --> 02:04:05.625
Kaana Baba's Ayurvedic oil.

1909
02:04:05.792 --> 02:04:08.042
The company shut down,
but the lice are still here.

1910
02:04:08.500 --> 02:04:11.042
So we thought,
if this oil can get rid of ghosts,

1911
02:04:11.125 --> 02:04:12.805
then surely it can help with our lice too.

1912
02:04:12.958 --> 02:04:14.639
You're using sacred oil to deal with lice?

1913
02:04:14.667 --> 02:04:17.792
You're lucky, Chotiya is not here.

1914
02:04:17.875 --> 02:04:18.875
Chotiya?

1915
02:04:18.917 --> 02:04:21.167
Chotiya, Junior Pundit.

1916
02:04:21.292 --> 02:04:24.208
Or else he would finish all your oil.

1917
02:04:26.167 --> 02:04:28.042
I'll finish both of you!

1918
02:04:28.417 --> 02:04:29.792
You are such a fool.

1919
02:04:29.875 --> 02:04:31.559
You are getting bashed up
with your own shoes!

1920
02:04:31.583 --> 02:04:33.042
Manjulika!

1921
02:04:33.833 --> 02:04:35.333
- Manjulika!
- Come on, let's go!

1922
02:04:35.417 --> 02:04:36.583
You oil thief!

1923
02:04:47.708 --> 02:04:48.708
Meera!

1924
02:04:55.583 --> 02:04:56.583
Meera!

1925
02:04:57.125 --> 02:04:58.125
Meera!

1926
02:05:01.708 --> 02:05:03.417
What are you doing, Meera?

1927
02:05:04.750 --> 02:05:08.458
I had a very bad dream.

1928
02:05:10.125 --> 02:05:11.125
I saw…

1929
02:05:12.583 --> 02:05:15.833
that I set myself on fire.

1930
02:05:17.542 --> 02:05:18.542
What?

1931
02:05:28.292 --> 02:05:29.292
Meera…

1932
02:05:30.833 --> 02:05:31.833
hand me that lighter.

1933
02:05:34.458 --> 02:05:36.417
You were just as scared
then as you are now.

1934
02:05:38.958 --> 02:05:39.958
Meera,

1935
02:05:40.458 --> 02:05:41.818
if something happens to you, then…

1936
02:05:42.292 --> 02:05:43.458
Then let's die together.

1937
02:05:46.875 --> 02:05:47.875
Yes,

1938
02:05:48.708 --> 02:05:49.708
let's do it together.

1939
02:05:50.625 --> 02:05:51.625
I'm coming.

1940
02:05:52.167 --> 02:05:53.167
Come here.

1941
02:05:53.667 --> 02:05:54.667
I'm coming.

1942
02:05:55.583 --> 02:05:56.583
Come on.

1943
02:06:00.708 --> 02:06:02.583
- Let me go!
- Meera…

1944
02:06:02.667 --> 02:06:04.208
- Let me go!
- Meera…

1945
02:06:04.292 --> 02:06:06.417
Meera!

1946
02:06:15.250 --> 02:06:16.917
- What happened to you?
- I…

1947
02:06:17.833 --> 02:06:19.000
I was…

1948
02:06:20.333 --> 02:06:21.875
I was with Mandira.

1949
02:06:22.167 --> 02:06:24.208
How did I end up here?

1950
02:06:27.167 --> 02:06:28.167
Mandira!

1951
02:06:28.708 --> 02:06:29.708
Ruhaan!

1952
02:06:29.917 --> 02:06:31.125
- Mandira!
- Ruhaan!

1953
02:06:48.625 --> 02:06:49.625
Mandira!

1954
02:06:50.583 --> 02:06:52.417
- Ruhaan?
- What is your problem?

1955
02:06:53.292 --> 02:06:54.292
What happened, Ruhaan?

1956
02:06:54.333 --> 02:06:55.643
You have a problem with me, right?

1957
02:06:55.667 --> 02:06:56.907
Why did you drag Meera into it?

1958
02:06:57.292 --> 02:06:58.292
Meera…

1959
02:07:00.000 --> 02:07:01.000
I didn't get you.

1960
02:07:01.167 --> 02:07:02.417
Cut the crap.

1961
02:07:03.208 --> 02:07:05.089
You were waiting for Durga Ashtami,
weren't you?

1962
02:07:05.333 --> 02:07:06.333
Today is Durga Ashtami.

1963
02:07:07.458 --> 02:07:10.167
Either you kill me or I will kill you.

1964
02:07:10.250 --> 02:07:12.375
Come on, get on with it.
Let's get started.

1965
02:07:12.458 --> 02:07:14.417
What are you doing?
Have you gone crazy or what?

1966
02:07:14.500 --> 02:07:16.250
- Ruhaan!
- Don't interfere!

1967
02:07:16.417 --> 02:07:18.417
- Ruhaan.
- The cleaned painting is back.

1968
02:07:18.500 --> 02:07:20.000
- I'll...
- Have a look!

1969
02:07:31.208 --> 02:07:32.833
PRINCESS MANJULIKA

1970
02:07:39.125 --> 02:07:40.125
Let me go.

1971
02:07:41.458 --> 02:07:42.458
Let me go!

1972
02:07:44.792 --> 02:07:49.750
I am Manjulika!

1973
02:07:52.833 --> 02:07:53.667
Let me go!

1974
02:07:53.750 --> 02:07:55.333
Let me go!

1975
02:07:55.625 --> 02:07:56.625
Should I?

1976
02:07:57.042 --> 02:07:58.500
There you go then.

1977
02:08:04.792 --> 02:08:08.708
I'll first kill our dear brother,
then I'll kill you.

1978
02:08:14.417 --> 02:08:17.000
What are you looking at, my dear brother?

1979
02:08:17.208 --> 02:08:18.583
I'm coming.

1980
02:08:19.125 --> 02:08:20.333
I'm coming for you.

1981
02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:32.292
Oh, my precious…

1982
02:08:33.125 --> 02:08:34.625
does that hurt?

1983
02:08:35.417 --> 02:08:38.250
Okay, then let's put an end to it.

1984
02:08:38.333 --> 02:08:39.333
Ruhaan!

1985
02:08:40.583 --> 02:08:43.917
I'm going to kill you!

1986
02:09:18.917 --> 02:09:19.917
Are you okay?

1987
02:09:20.083 --> 02:09:21.083
Yes.

1988
02:09:21.667 --> 02:09:22.667
Hey…

1989
02:09:23.000 --> 02:09:24.417
Ms. Mandira, I'm sorry.

1990
02:09:24.875 --> 02:09:25.875
I misunderstood you.

1991
02:09:26.208 --> 02:09:27.208
Are you fine?

1992
02:09:36.833 --> 02:09:38.792
I'm absolutely fine now.

1993
02:09:53.083 --> 02:09:55.250
You set the wrong sister on fire.

1994
02:09:55.875 --> 02:09:56.875
Help!

1995
02:09:57.375 --> 02:09:59.042
I'm Manjulika!

1996
02:09:59.292 --> 02:10:01.167
I'm Manjulika!

1997
02:10:17.167 --> 02:10:20.583
This is my throne! It's mine!

1998
02:10:25.250 --> 02:10:27.000
Help!

1999
02:10:28.000 --> 02:10:30.167
This is how I had cried out in anguish,

2000
02:10:30.750 --> 02:10:33.292
but everyone simply
stood there and watched.

2001
02:10:33.417 --> 02:10:35.625
Today, all of you will scream,

2002
02:10:35.917 --> 02:10:38.042
and I will relish the spectacle.

2003
02:10:38.125 --> 02:10:39.125
Manjulika!

2004
02:10:40.167 --> 02:10:41.917
What powers are you so boastful of?

2005
02:10:42.917 --> 02:10:44.542
You will face your end today!

2006
02:10:49.458 --> 02:10:50.458
Raj Purohit?

2007
02:10:50.792 --> 02:10:51.792
Brother.

2008
02:10:54.083 --> 02:10:56.958
Why did he have to fall here?

2009
02:10:58.083 --> 02:11:00.958
Now all her attention
is on our family.

2010
02:11:01.042 --> 02:11:02.250
Do something!

2011
02:11:04.750 --> 02:11:07.708
Ms. Manjulika,
please don't come near us.

2012
02:11:07.792 --> 02:11:11.167
We have sacred oil in our hair.
Look.

2013
02:11:13.750 --> 02:11:15.250
Ask him.

2014
02:11:15.333 --> 02:11:16.476
He's the one who provided
us with the oil.

2015
02:11:16.500 --> 02:11:17.809
- Tell her!
- I didn't give it to you!

2016
02:11:17.833 --> 02:11:20.042
You two stole it, you oil thieves!

2017
02:11:29.167 --> 02:11:30.167
Faulad Singh!

2018
02:11:30.500 --> 02:11:31.583
Protect us!

2019
02:11:31.875 --> 02:11:32.708
Forget it!

2020
02:11:32.792 --> 02:11:34.125
Who's going to protect me?

2021
02:11:34.667 --> 02:11:36.583
Oh God!

2022
02:11:36.667 --> 02:11:37.667
Oh God!

2023
02:11:40.833 --> 02:11:43.958
Oh God, help us.

2024
02:12:07.208 --> 02:12:08.625
- Chauhan?
- Hey…

2025
02:12:09.792 --> 02:12:11.958
Not Chauhan, Jawan.

2026
02:12:14.875 --> 02:12:15.875
Jawan?

2027
02:12:16.083 --> 02:12:17.250
Jawan!

2028
02:12:17.375 --> 02:12:18.375
Jawan?!

2029
02:12:27.042 --> 02:12:28.042
<i>Ready?</i>

2030
02:12:28.708 --> 02:12:30.292
Nice jump, Jawan.

2031
02:12:30.500 --> 02:12:31.917
You're our only hope now.

2032
02:12:37.917 --> 02:12:39.875
What kind of Jawan is he?

2033
02:12:40.167 --> 02:12:42.333
He can't even stand up with the support.

2034
02:12:46.833 --> 02:12:47.667
Chotiya?

2035
02:12:47.750 --> 02:12:50.667
Oh no, he's our Chotiya.
Junior Pundit.

2036
02:12:50.750 --> 02:12:52.167
What are you saying?!

2037
02:12:55.833 --> 02:12:57.667
- Junior Pundit!
- Junior Pundit?

2038
02:12:58.125 --> 02:12:59.208
Who's that?

2039
02:12:59.292 --> 02:13:01.000
He's lost his memory.

2040
02:13:01.292 --> 02:13:03.083
Memory? What's that?

2041
02:13:06.167 --> 02:13:07.167
She'll help you remember.

2042
02:13:08.333 --> 02:13:09.333
Ms. Mallika.

2043
02:13:09.583 --> 02:13:10.583
Ms. Mallika.

2044
02:13:11.750 --> 02:13:12.750
Help me remember.

2045
02:13:16.333 --> 02:13:17.333
Ruhaan.

2046
02:13:39.667 --> 02:13:40.667
Ruhaan!

2047
02:13:43.833 --> 02:13:45.125
The mistake you made with me,

2048
02:13:45.625 --> 02:13:46.875
don't repeat it with her.

2049
02:13:51.083 --> 02:13:53.167
The secret I never uncovered in my life

2050
02:13:53.958 --> 02:13:57.042
came back to me when I faced death.

2051
02:14:06.667 --> 02:14:07.875
The truth is,

2052
02:14:09.292 --> 02:14:11.250
neither I nor she is a ghost.

2053
02:14:15.042 --> 02:14:16.042
It is time.

2054
02:14:17.542 --> 02:14:20.542
Step forward and reveal
your true self to everyone.

2055
02:15:43.042 --> 02:15:44.042
Manjulika?

2056
02:15:45.708 --> 02:15:46.833
No, not Manjulika,

2057
02:15:48.333 --> 02:15:50.167
I'm Prince Debendra Nath.

2058
02:16:51.292 --> 02:16:52.292
Debu,

2059
02:16:53.000 --> 02:16:54.958
is it you who dances
all night in the palace?

2060
02:16:55.542 --> 02:16:56.583
No…

2061
02:16:56.958 --> 02:16:57.958
No, Sister.

2062
02:16:58.333 --> 02:16:59.333
Never!

2063
02:17:00.292 --> 02:17:01.292
Why are you lying?

2064
02:17:01.917 --> 02:17:03.125
We saw you.

2065
02:17:04.333 --> 02:17:05.708
Why are you scared?

2066
02:17:06.125 --> 02:17:07.750
We won't tell anyone.

2067
02:17:08.708 --> 02:17:10.292
After all, we are your sisters.

2068
02:17:16.833 --> 02:17:17.833
Yes, Sister,

2069
02:17:18.375 --> 02:17:19.375
it's me.

2070
02:17:21.625 --> 02:17:24.667
Our Debu is such a great dancer, right?

2071
02:17:25.208 --> 02:17:26.583
So beautiful.

2072
02:17:27.708 --> 02:17:29.083
I love to dance.

2073
02:17:30.375 --> 02:17:31.458
I really do.

2074
02:17:31.708 --> 02:17:32.583
Really?

2075
02:17:32.708 --> 02:17:34.167
I don't want to be a king either.

2076
02:17:35.333 --> 02:17:36.375
Honestly,

2077
02:17:37.333 --> 02:17:39.958
I'm just like you on the inside.

2078
02:17:41.042 --> 02:17:42.333
I'm not Debendra Nath,

2079
02:17:43.500 --> 02:17:44.625
I'm Manjulika.

2080
02:17:46.375 --> 02:17:48.875
Come on then,
let's help you get ready today.

2081
02:17:49.417 --> 02:17:52.083
You'll dance, and we'll sing.

2082
02:17:53.042 --> 02:17:56.375
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

2083
02:17:57.125 --> 02:18:01.167
<i>To this sweet tune of love's enthrall</i>

2084
02:18:01.333 --> 02:18:04.667
<i>Oh my beloved, hear my call</i>

2085
02:18:05.458 --> 02:18:09.250
<i>My wishes</i>

2086
02:18:09.583 --> 02:18:13.417
<i>Will drift through the air</i>

2087
02:18:13.833 --> 02:18:17.208
The one you gave the throne simply
because he is a male,

2088
02:18:17.292 --> 02:18:19.333
just go and see what he's really like.

2089
02:18:31.375 --> 02:18:33.625
<i>I was simple, pure</i>

2090
02:18:33.708 --> 02:18:35.708
<i>Gullible and too trusting</i>

2091
02:18:35.792 --> 02:18:39.167
<i>I was naive for sure</i>

2092
02:18:39.792 --> 02:18:41.958
<i>Of the ways of the world unfair</i>

2093
02:18:42.042 --> 02:18:44.000
<i>Of wit's clever snare</i>

2094
02:18:44.083 --> 02:18:47.542
<i>I was unaware</i>

2095
02:18:47.875 --> 02:18:52.083
<i>My innocent heart was wounded so deep</i>

2096
02:18:52.292 --> 02:18:55.792
<i>It broke and shattered lost in its keep</i>

2097
02:18:56.167 --> 02:19:00.458
<i>The precious pearl that
Slipped from love's bind</i>

2098
02:19:00.542 --> 02:19:04.542
<i>Will never be fixed in time</i>

2099
02:19:04.792 --> 02:19:06.917
<i>Poisonous dreams</i>

2100
02:19:07.000 --> 02:19:09.083
<i>My own kin</i>

2101
02:19:09.167 --> 02:19:12.958
<i>Deceived me it seems</i>

2102
02:19:14.250 --> 02:19:17.208
Maharaja, what punishment
do you want to give him?

2103
02:19:22.625 --> 02:19:23.625
Death.

2104
02:19:24.292 --> 02:19:25.812
But what will we say to your subjects?

2105
02:19:25.917 --> 02:19:29.417
Proclaim throughout the kingdom
that Prince Debendra Nath is dead,

2106
02:19:30.458 --> 02:19:31.500
and that…

2107
02:19:33.792 --> 02:19:35.083
Manjulika killed him.

2108
02:19:35.875 --> 02:19:36.875
Me?

2109
02:19:37.583 --> 02:19:40.625
You both could have
told me this in private.

2110
02:19:42.458 --> 02:19:44.667
But you had to put on this drama
in front of everyone

2111
02:19:44.750 --> 02:19:47.208
because of your greed for the throne.

2112
02:19:47.417 --> 02:19:49.917
You made your brother dance like that.

2113
02:19:51.042 --> 02:19:55.375
None of my children deserves this throne.

2114
02:19:58.042 --> 02:19:59.042
From now on,

2115
02:19:59.667 --> 02:20:02.375
you will be known as
your brother's murderer.

2116
02:20:04.375 --> 02:20:05.583
And Anjulika,

2117
02:20:06.625 --> 02:20:10.875
your name will be erased
from the pages of history.

2118
02:20:12.875 --> 02:20:16.125
I'm sentencing both of you to exile.

2119
02:20:44.250 --> 02:20:48.417
<i>My body was incomplete</i>

2120
02:20:49.250 --> 02:20:52.708
<i>A mere shadow's trace</i>

2121
02:20:53.375 --> 02:20:57.083
<i>The home once my paradise turned</i>

2122
02:20:57.583 --> 02:21:00.958
<i>To a hellish place</i>

2123
02:21:01.042 --> 02:21:05.667
<i>My body was incomplete</i>

2124
02:21:06.000 --> 02:21:10.083
<i>A mere shadow's trace</i>

2125
02:21:10.167 --> 02:21:14.167
<i>The home once my paradise turned</i>

2126
02:21:14.333 --> 02:21:17.125
<i>To a hellish place</i>

2127
02:21:17.417 --> 02:21:21.542
<i>These thrones and crowns
I'll burn them all</i>

2128
02:21:21.625 --> 02:21:25.625
<i>No one will survive
I'll end them all</i>

2129
02:21:25.750 --> 02:21:29.917
<i>This body may perish
But the soul will not fade</i>

2130
02:21:30.000 --> 02:21:34.208
<i>No matter the torment
It'll never be afraid</i>

2131
02:21:59.625 --> 02:22:01.375
I'll set up a similar protective shield

2132
02:22:01.500 --> 02:22:04.500
at the entrance to
Princess Manjulika's room

2133
02:22:04.583 --> 02:22:06.792
to indicate to the people

2134
02:22:07.167 --> 02:22:09.875
that her spirit is held captive there.

2135
02:22:10.458 --> 02:22:14.333
It's crucial that no one learns
that the actual spirit is not Manjulika's,

2136
02:22:14.875 --> 02:22:16.875
but Prince Debendra Nath's,

2137
02:22:17.208 --> 02:22:18.750
who is imprisoned here.

2138
02:22:22.583 --> 02:22:24.792
For years,
I've been confined behind that door,

2139
02:22:24.875 --> 02:22:28.000
seething with the urge
for revenge against you both.

2140
02:22:29.750 --> 02:22:32.250
When I finally came out,
both of you were there.

2141
02:22:33.333 --> 02:22:35.917
I intended to kill you both
on the very first night.

2142
02:22:36.833 --> 02:22:37.833
I wanted you dead!

2143
02:22:47.833 --> 02:22:48.917
Then I thought

2144
02:22:49.708 --> 02:22:51.958
it would be a quick
and easy end for you.

2145
02:22:53.583 --> 02:22:55.250
You too should die

2146
02:22:56.500 --> 02:22:58.125
as I did.

2147
02:22:59.833 --> 02:23:01.542
You should be burned alive.

2148
02:23:02.958 --> 02:23:05.708
You both were plotting
against me last time.

2149
02:23:06.208 --> 02:23:07.375
This time, it was my turn.

2150
02:23:07.458 --> 02:23:09.750
Mine!

2151
02:23:15.167 --> 02:23:16.167
He died.

2152
02:23:17.625 --> 02:23:20.708
Gradually, I convinced everyone

2153
02:23:21.458 --> 02:23:24.708
that you two were Manjulika.

2154
02:23:35.458 --> 02:23:37.167
I said I don't visit temples!

2155
02:23:39.208 --> 02:23:41.958
I'm Manjulika!

2156
02:23:42.042 --> 02:23:44.000
I'm Manjulika!

2157
02:23:44.500 --> 02:23:48.833
Today, on Durga Ashtami,
everyone would have first set me on fire,

2158
02:23:50.542 --> 02:23:51.542
then you.

2159
02:23:53.000 --> 02:23:54.167
But that couldn't happen.

2160
02:23:58.208 --> 02:23:59.250
It's alright.

2161
02:24:00.000 --> 02:24:01.792
All of you will burn!

2162
02:24:02.500 --> 02:24:04.708
All of you will burn alive!

2163
02:25:03.958 --> 02:25:05.208
Raj Purohit!

2164
02:25:06.042 --> 02:25:07.333
What will you do now?

2165
02:25:08.375 --> 02:25:10.375
How will you protect the royal family now?

2166
02:25:11.542 --> 02:25:14.375
Focus on how you'll ensure
your own survival first.

2167
02:25:15.292 --> 02:25:17.708
Look down and see
where you're standing right now.

2168
02:25:49.708 --> 02:25:51.708
Don't burn me.

2169
02:25:51.792 --> 02:25:52.625
Stay away!

2170
02:25:52.708 --> 02:25:53.708
Stay away!

2171
02:25:54.208 --> 02:25:55.208
I won't burn!

2172
02:26:03.375 --> 02:26:04.375
Burn him!

2173
02:26:06.250 --> 02:26:09.500
It's the two of you who have
been reincarnated, not Ruhaan.

2174
02:26:12.292 --> 02:26:13.772
Set him ablaze and turn him to ashes.

2175
02:26:14.917 --> 02:26:15.917
Stay away!

2176
02:26:17.750 --> 02:26:18.958
Stay away!
I won't spare you!

2177
02:26:21.958 --> 02:26:23.000
Stay away!

2178
02:26:26.875 --> 02:26:27.875
I won't spare you!

2179
02:26:33.417 --> 02:26:35.167
I completely trust both of you, Sister.

2180
02:26:42.167 --> 02:26:44.375
Who else would understand me
if not my sisters?

2181
02:26:49.708 --> 02:26:51.083
I love you both very much.

2182
02:27:15.917 --> 02:27:19.292
We didn't reincarnate
to repeat our past mistakes…

2183
02:27:20.125 --> 02:27:21.625
we came back to make things right.

2184
02:27:25.458 --> 02:27:26.875
We were envious of you,

2185
02:27:29.125 --> 02:27:30.708
and because of that jealousy,

2186
02:27:31.292 --> 02:27:33.375
everyone set you ablaze.

2187
02:27:36.250 --> 02:27:37.792
You were always trapped.

2188
02:27:40.042 --> 02:27:41.958
In a man's body when you were alive,

2189
02:27:43.042 --> 02:27:46.208
and behind that door after you died.

2190
02:27:47.583 --> 02:27:48.875
We never truly understood you.

2191
02:27:49.875 --> 02:27:51.083
Please forgive us, Brother.

2192
02:27:54.083 --> 02:27:55.250
Forgive us, Debu.

2193
02:27:57.417 --> 02:28:00.708
If punishing us brings you closure,

2194
02:28:01.417 --> 02:28:03.083
then go ahead and kill us,
set us ablaze.

2195
02:28:04.167 --> 02:28:06.667
But let these people go.

2196
02:28:07.625 --> 02:28:08.946
They haven't done anything wrong.

2197
02:29:23.500 --> 02:29:24.500
What's happening?

2198
02:29:26.042 --> 02:29:27.042
He found salvation.

2199
02:29:33.250 --> 02:29:34.667
My ancestors were right.

2200
02:29:36.083 --> 02:29:38.875
Someone from the royal family
must reincarnate to put an end to this.

2201
02:29:43.208 --> 02:29:45.042
But I didn't realize that the resolution

2202
02:29:46.583 --> 02:29:48.208
wouldn't come by setting him ablaze,

2203
02:29:49.667 --> 02:29:50.792
but by understanding him.

2204
02:31:04.125 --> 02:31:06.625
Since I was a child,
I've been having visions of this palace.

2205
02:31:07.208 --> 02:31:11.917
I knew I had some connection to it,

2206
02:31:12.583 --> 02:31:15.792
which is why I began
restoring old palaces.

2207
02:31:16.500 --> 02:31:20.042
I thought maybe I'd learn
something about this palace someday.

2208
02:31:21.125 --> 02:31:22.500
But when the chance arose,

2209
02:31:22.792 --> 02:31:25.417
the company assigned
Mr. Kaushik instead of me.

2210
02:31:25.542 --> 02:31:28.042
So that's why you…

2211
02:31:29.208 --> 02:31:31.292
Are you crazy?
Why would I kill him?

2212
02:31:31.750 --> 02:31:34.000
But you said he went on a long break.

2213
02:31:34.167 --> 02:31:36.750
He actually did go
on a long break to Goa.

2214
02:31:37.000 --> 02:31:38.292
- Oh.
- Oh!

2215
02:31:38.708 --> 02:31:40.833
I came here for a different reason too.

2216
02:31:41.625 --> 02:31:44.708
But I also started
to feel something once I got here.

2217
02:31:45.208 --> 02:31:47.449
So, you weren't here
to purchase the palace, Ms. Mandira?

2218
02:31:48.750 --> 02:31:50.292
My name isn't even Mandira.

2219
02:31:50.750 --> 02:31:51.750
Then what is it?

2220
02:31:52.958 --> 02:31:53.958
ACP Rathore.

2221
02:31:55.125 --> 02:31:56.167
ACP Rathore?

2222
02:31:58.833 --> 02:32:00.042
ACP Rathore!

2223
02:32:01.417 --> 02:32:02.583
Madhuri…
